\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Japan \highlight\uc2  MOF Data Show No  \highlight22\uc2 FX Intervention \highlight\uc2  June 29-July 27\b0\par\par\uc2 289 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Juli 2011\par 12:17\par \uc2 Dow Jones Business News\par \uc2 DJON\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 TOKYO -(Dow Jones)- \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  authorities didn't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market in the June 29-July 27 period, data released by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  showed Friday.\par \par \uc2 The data confirm that the Japanese government was not behind three sudden drops in the yen in Asian trading hours during the period. Some market participants had said \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  could not be ruled out as a cause of those yen falls, though most believe the moves were caused by the triggering of stop-loss orders and other investors piling onto the sudden moves.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  last \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  four months ago after the dollar dropped to a post World War II-low of Y76.25 on March 17, a week after the March 11 earthquake and tsunami. The disaster pressured the yen up in part by encouraging speculation Japanese firms operating overseas would send money back to Japan to meet reconstruction and other costs.\par \par \uc2 In its yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  at that time, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold Y692.5 billion, following a rare declaration of joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Group of Seven economic powers. The strong yen hurts Japan's key export sector by making their products less competitive overseas and eating into earnings sent back to Japan.\par \par \uc2 Friday's data cover trades settled in July. Trades in the spot market are settled after two business days.\par \par \uc2 During the period covered, the dollar traded in a Y77.57-Y81.49 range. The greenback dropped even lower Friday, touching a fresh four-month low at Y77.44 in Asian trading hours.\par \par \uc2 -By Andrew Monahan, Dow Jones Newswires; 81-3-6269-2783; andrew.monahan@dowjones.com [ 07-29-11 0617ET ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJON000020110729e77t0002w\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
