\par\par \b \uc2 Aichi Gov: Fall In Dollar Below Y80 Making Conditions Difficult For Japan Manufacturers\b0\par\par\uc2 479 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Juli 2011\par 09:38\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 -- Governor of Aichi prefecture says dollar below Y80 is making conditions difficult for Japanese manufacturers\par \par \uc2 -- Says \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  should conduct joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  with G-7 partners\par \par \uc2 -- Told by economy minister any \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would need to be large to succeed in weakening the yen\par \par \uc2 -- BOJ directly buying government debt for reconstruction is one option to ease policy further\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    By Takashi Mochizuki \par    Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 TOKYO (Dow Jones)--Hideaki Ohmura, governor of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Toyota Motor Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 .'s home base of Aichi prefecture, said Friday the central government and the Bank of Japan should take aggressive action to lower the excessively high level of the yen.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "The current yen strength is excessive and does not reflect Japanese economic fundamentals," Ohmura told Dow Jones Newswires. "I think it's hard for firms to manufacture goods domestically when the dollar is below Y80," he said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Hit by concerns over U.S. debt, the dollar fell Friday to Y77.44, its lowest level since a post-war record low of Y76.25 set March 17.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The governor's two-day trip to Tokyo was undertaken partly to demand strong yen-weakening measures to the administration of Prime Minister Naoto Kan and to the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 During his stay, Ohmura met with Economic and Fiscal Policy Minister Kaoru Yosano, Chief Cabinet Secretary Yukio Edano and BOJ Deputy Gov. Kiyohiko Nishimura.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "I'm upset because the government and the BOJ haven't issued any clear messages to the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market at a time when the economy is at risk," Ohmura said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The governor said the finance ministry should conduct joint \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  with its G-7 counterpart nations as was the case in March, just after northern Japan's devastating earthquake and tsunami.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Ohmura said chief spokesman Edano didn't provide the government's views on potential \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , but quoted Yosano as saying any \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  would need to be large.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Ohmura said a reported remark quoting Yosano as saying he is reluctant to undertake a large-scale \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  campaign is "completely false."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 On Thursday, some local media reported that Ohmura cited Yosano as saying undertaking an \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Y1 trillion to Y2 trillion would be difficult. Although Yosano isn't in charge of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  policy, the remark sent the yen higher against the dollar.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "I did not make any such comment and did not even mention any figures," Ohmura said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 As for the Bank of Japan, the governor demanded more aggressive easing, which has previously been rejected by senior \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  officials.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "I personally think if the government is going to issue debt for reconstruction, the BOJ may want to purchase them directly," he said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The BOJ is concerned such a move would invite higher yields.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Takashi Mochizuki, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-6269-2782; takashi.mochizuki@dowjones.com [ 29-07-11 0740GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 4258 5095   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110729e77t000zb\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
