\par\par \b \uc2 Dow Jones Asia-Pacific Top Stories Sked For July 28\b0\par\par\uc2 3,056 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Juli 2011\par 09:13\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 Following are the top Asia-Pacific stories featured on Dow Jones Newswires as of 0700 GMT. Not all stories appear on all wires. Please direct any questions or comments to asianewseds@dowjones.com.\par \par \uc2 MACRO/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 /FIXED INCOME:\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: CHINA \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  REGULATOR: RESERVE BUILDUP NOT MAJOR CAUSE OF INFLATION \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  regulator released its third statement in just over a week refuting criticisms of its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  management, saying that the accumulation of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves is not a major cause of inflation. (published 0328 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par JAPAN MOF RAISES VIEW OF ECONOMY FOR APRIL-JUNE, 1ST UPGRADE IN 4 QUARTERS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's finance minister Yoshihiko Noda said Thursday his ministry will say in a quarterly report to be released later in the day that the economy was "still in a tough spot due to the effects of the Great East Japan Earthquake, but was showing some positive signs" in the April-June quarter. (published 0114 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par 2ND UPDATE: SOUTH KOREA JUNE CURRENT-ACCOUNT SURPLUS AT 8-MONTH HIGH \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korea's current-account surplus rose in June to its highest level in eight months on strong exports of automobiles and steel products, providing further support to the strengthening local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . (published 0116 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: TAIWAN PRESIDENT SEES WEAKER GLOBAL ECONOMY IN 2H \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Taiwan President Ma Ying-jeou on Thursday voiced concerns that debt problems in the U.S. and Europe could slow global economic growth in the second half of this year, potentially affecting Taiwan's export-reliant economy. (published 0607 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par 2ND UPDATE: RBNZ HOLDS STEADY BUT SIGNALS INTENT TO HIKE SOON \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 New Zealand's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Thursday stood pat as expected but indicated it is looking to take back an emergency rate cut implemented in March after the Christchurch earthquake, prompting economists to dial forward their forecasts for a rate hike to September. (published 0327 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ANZ BANK\f28 \uc2 \f2  EXPECTS AUSTRALIA RATE HIKE NEXT WEEK \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australia's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will hike interest rates 25 basis points when it meets next week, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Australia & New Zealand Banking Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Thursday. (published 0454 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: INDIA MAY EXCEED FISCAL-GAP AIM; NO RATING CHANGE YET - S&P \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 India may exceed its budget-deficit target for the current financial year but that doesn't warrant any rating revision as the government aims to stick to medium-term fiscal rigor, a \f28 \uc2 \f2 Standard & Poor's\f28 \uc2 \f2  executive said. (published 0632 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par DATA SNAP: INDIA PRIMARY ARTICLES WPI STEADY IN WEEK TO JULY 16 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The wholesale price index for primary articles in India was little-changed at 198.0 in the week ended July 16, compared to a provisional 197.7 in the previous week, according to data issued Thursday by the Ministry of Commerce and Industry. (published 0632 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par ADB: ASIA SHOULDN'T OVERREACT TO SLOWDOWN IN ADVANCED ECONOMIES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Emerging east Asian economies shouldn't abruptly ease off on the policy-tightening brakes due to weakness in the advanced world, and some nations may need to move faster, not slower, to remove crisis-era stimulus, the Asian Development Bank said Thursday. (published 0200 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: CHINA RESEARCHER URGES GOVERNMENT TO SELL DOLLAR ASSETS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China should reduce its dollar-denominated assets as soon as possible to safeguard its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves, a government researcher said Thursday, as the impasse over raising the U.S. debt limit dragged on in Washington. (published 0127 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA 2011 TRADE SURPLUS LIKELY TO FALL 14% TO $157B - THINK TANK \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's trade surplus is likely to narrow 14% to $157 billion in 2011 from a year earlier, a government think tank said Thursday. (published 2326 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par INDONESIA 2Q GDP GROWTH LIKELY 'NOT LESS' THAN 6.5% ON YEAR - CHIEF STATISTICIAN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Indonesia's economic growth in the second quarter was likely "not less" than the first quarter's expansion of 6.5% from a year earlier, supported by strong exports and investment spending, Chief Statistician Rusman Heriawan said Thursday. (published 0553 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par JAPAN FINANCE MINISTER: CONTINUE TO PAY ATTENTION TO MARKET MOVEMENTS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's Finance Minister said Thursday that he will continue to watch movements in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market, adding that he is aware of concerns among exporters about the strength of the yen. (published 0024 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par JAPAN JUN OVERALL RETAIL SALES +1.1% ON YEAR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japanese retail sales rose 1.1% in June from a year earlier, the Ministry of Economy, Trade and Industry said Thursday. (published 0001 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: 2-YEAR JGB AUCTION STRONG AS US DEBT IMPASSE HELPS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 An auction of two-year Japanese government bonds met with solid demand Thursday, as concerns that the continued U.S. debt ceiling impasse could roil global markets added to demand from Japanese banks and other financial institutions, already major buyers of the tenor. (published 0454 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par THAI JUNE INDUSTRIAL PRODUCTION INDEX RISES 3.3% ON YEAR - OFFICIAL \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Thailand's industrial production index rose 3.3% from a year earlier to 200.64 in June, an official at the Ministry of Industry's Office of Industrial Economics said Thursday. (published 0457 GMT)\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  ASIA: PUSH BY CORPORATE \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 JAPAN\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  FOR WEAKER YEN RATCHETS UP \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  CHANCES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 With Japanese exporters increasingly demanding an end to the recent sharp gains in the yen, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dealers say pressure is growing on the government to launch yen-selling \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , although the chances of success are seen as uncertain at best. (published 0557 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 EQUITIES:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par SONY SLIDES TO 1Q NET LOSS ON QUAKE, CUTS FY GUIDANCE AS YEN STRENGTHENS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Sony Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Thursday that it swung to a net loss in the fiscal first quarter ended June on the impact of the March 11 earthquake and tsunami on production and lowered its earnings forecast for the fiscal year on the recent rise in the yen versus other major \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . (published 0618 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par TOSHIBA 1Q GROUP NET PROFIT Y470.00M, UP 0.9% ON YR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Toshiba Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Thursday that its net profit rose slightly in the fiscal first quarter as lower restructuring costs and solid energy-saving appliance sales in Japan lessened the sting that the March 11 disaster had on the company's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . (published 0618 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 HYUNDAI MOTOR\f28 \uc2 \f2  2Q NET PROFIT AT UP 37% ON YEAR AT KRW2.307 TLN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Hyundai Motor Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., South Korea's biggest car maker by sales, said Thursday its second-quarter net profit surged 37% from a year earlier due to strong sales of its fuel-efficient vehicles in overseas markets and stronger contributions from its affiliates. (published 0510 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par PANASONIC SWINGS INTO 1Q NET LOSS, KEEPS FY PROFIT OUTLOOK \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Panasonic Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Thursday it swung to a net loss in the three months through June, as the lingering impact from the March 11 earthquake and tsunami hurt domestic production. (published 0658 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: PANASONIC TO SELL SANYO'S HOME APPLIANCE BUSINESS TO HAIER-SOURCE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Panasonic Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . plans to sell subsidiary \f28 \uc2 \f2 Sanyo Electric Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 .'s household appliance businesses to the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Haier Group\f28 \uc2 \f2 , a person familiar with the matter said Thursday, in a rare move for a Japanese electronics conglomerate to let a rising Chinese rival take over a chunk of its major business segment. (published 0151 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par FUJITSU SLIPS TO 1Q NET LOSS ON QUAKE, STILL SEES STRONG 2H REBOUND \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Fujitsu Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Thursday that it swung to a net loss in the three months through June from a year-earlier profit, hurt like most of its peers in the technology sector by absorbing costs related to the March 11 disasters. (published 0633 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par 2ND UPDATE: DBS GROUP 2Q NET BETTER THAN EXPECTED, LOANS INCOME IMPROVES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 DBS Group Holdings Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . swung to a slightly-better-than-expected second-quarter net profit as the Singapore-listed bank continued to improve its earnings on loans and reversed its impairment-related loss from a year earlier. (published 0612 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par TSMC 2ND-QUARTER NET PROFIT DOWN 10.7% AT NT$35.95 BLN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Taiwan Semiconductor Manufacturing Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Thursday its second-quarter net profit fell 10.7% from a year earlier, and the company has scaled back its capacity expansion plan for this year due to weakening global demand for chips. (published 0545 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: \f28 \uc2 \f2 CHEUNG KONG INFRASTRUCTURE\f28 \uc2 \f2  1ST-HALF NET NEARLY DOUBLES TO HK$3.98 BLN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Cheung Kong Infrastructure Holdings Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., a utility and infrastructure company controlled by tycoon Li Ka-shing, said Thursday its first-half net profit nearly doubled from a year earlier, boosted by contributions from the U.K. electricity assets it acquired last year. (published 0527 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par 2ND UPDATE: WESFARMERS SAYS AUSTRALIA'S RETAIL SECTOR IS STRUGGLING \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australia's beleaguered retail sector continues to struggle against a backdrop of declining consumer confidence, falling prices and natural disasters, conglomerate \f28 \uc2 \f2 Wesfarmers Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Thursday. (published 0345 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par 2ND UPDATE: MACQUARIE TIPS WEAKER 1H PROFIT, INVESTOR CONFIDENCE FRAGILE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Macquarie Group Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . on Thursday forecast a weaker first half profit, citing fragile investor confidence, and warned that a U.S. debt default could take the global economy into dangerous unchartered territory. (published 0614 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 LOGITECH\f28 \uc2 \f2  SWINGS TO $29.6 MILLION 1Q NET LOSS; CEO QUINDLEN STEPS DOWN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Computer peripherals maker \f28 \uc2 \f2 Logitech International SA\f28 \uc2 \f2  fell short of expectations Thursday by posting a first quarter net loss of $29.6 million and lowered its sales outlook for the full fiscal year to approximately $2.5 billion from $2.6 billion. (published 0226 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par DAEWOO SHIPBUILDING 2Q NET DOWN 3.6% ON \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  LOSSES, OPERATING PROFIT SURGES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Daewoo Shipbuilding & Marine Engineering Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., the world's No. 3 shipbuilder by sales, said Thursday its second-quarter net profit fell 3.6% due to foreign-\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  losses as a result of the strong won. (published 0137 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: \f28 \uc2 \f2 KOREAN AIR\f28 \uc2 \f2  SHIFTS TO NET PROFIT ON \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  GAINS; STRONG 3Q EYED \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Korean Air Lines Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . swung to a net profit in the second quarter compared on foreign-\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  gains, but slid to an operating loss as a result of high fuel costs and decreased travel to Japan following the March 11 disasters, it said Thursday. (published 0254 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par WSJ: FORD TO BUILD ITS SECOND INDIA FACTORY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 28-07-11 0713GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Ford Motor Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . is doubling down on India. (published 0448 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: \f28 \uc2 \f2 LI & FUNG\f28 \uc2 \f2  FALLS 4.4%; CONCERNS ABOUT U.S. ECONOMY, BUSINESS MODEL \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Shares of supply chain manager \f28 \uc2 \f2 Li & Fung Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . were leading blue chips lower in Hong Kong Thursday amid continued worries about the U.S. economy--its key export market--and concerns about its business model given inflationary pressures. (published 0547 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par TIGER AIRWAYS: AUSTRALIA FLIGHT SUSPENSION HEARING ADJOURNED TO AUG 1 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Tiger Airways Holdings Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Thursday its Australian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will remain grounded until Aug. 1 after Australia's Federal Court adjourned a hearing on the suspension to that date. (published 0046 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par SOFTBANK 1Q GRP NET PROFIT SURGES ON SOLID MOBILE REVENUE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Softbank Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Thursday that its net profit for the three months through June surged nearly five-fold as Japan's only mobile carrier for \f28 \uc2 \f2 Apple Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2 .'s iPhone and iPad continued to enjoy solid revenue and a growing subscriber base. (published 0627 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 JAPAN TOBACCO\f28 \uc2 \f2  APR-JUNE GROUP NET PFT Y22.7B VS Y22.1B \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan Tobacco Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Thursday that its net profit for the fiscal first quarter ended June grew 2.4% on year, despite the disruption of some tobacco sales after the March 11 natural disasters. (published 0627 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par SAMSUNG SDI 2Q NET PROFIT UP 26.4% ON HIGHER EQUITY GAINS FROM MOBILE DISPLAY JV \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Samsung SDI Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Thursday its second-quarter net profit rose 26.4% from a year earlier period, largely thanks to higher investment gains from its joint venture, Samsung Mobile Display. (published 0503 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CITY DEVELOPMENTS: UNIT BUYS CHINA MIXED-USE LAND SITE FOR CNY886 MLN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 City Developments Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Thursday its unit has bought a mixed-use land site in China's eastern Jiangsu province for CNY886 million . (published 0000 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par SUN ART RAISES EXTRA HK$1.24 BLN IN HK VIA OVERALLOTMENT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Sun Art Retail Group Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Wednesday it will fully exercise the over-allotment option in its initial public offering to raise an additional HK$1.24 billion, bringing the total amount raised to US$1.22 billion. (published 0021 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 MAPLETREE INDUSTRIAL TRUST\f28 \uc2 \f2  PRICES PRIVATE PLACEMENT, PREFERENTIAL OFFERING \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Mapletree Industrial Trust Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Thursday it has priced the new units it plans to issue via private placement and preferential offering, in a follow-on equity fund raising that could raise about S$177 million. (published 2321 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CSR CORP UNVEILS $1.1 BLN OF CONTRACTS AFTER CHINA TRAIN ACCIDENT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 CSR Corp., which built one of the trains involved in a deadly train collision in eastern China, said Thursday it has received six contracts worth CNY6.9 billion from local and overseas firms to provide locomotives. (published 0035 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: PHILEX EXPECTS 2011 NET TO HIT NEW HIGH; 1H PROFIT MORE THAN TRIPLED \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Philex Mining Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Thursday it expects full-year net profit to hit a new high after reporting first-half earnings more than tripled, fuelled by record-high gold and copper prices. (published 0522 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par ALIBABA GROUP: PHONE WITH ALIBABA OPERATING SYSTEM TO LAUNCH IN JULY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Alibaba Group Holding Ltd. unit Alibaba Cloud Computing will release a mobile phone with an Alibaba-developed operating system late this month, the company said Thursday. (published 0624 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 UBS\f28 \uc2 \f2  SETS UP UNIT TO TAP CHINA PRIVATE EQUITY MARKET \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 UBS AG unit \f28 \uc2 \f2 UBS\f28 \uc2 \f2  Global Asset Management said Thursday it set up an asset management company in Beijing to tap China's rapidly growing market for private equity investment and advisory services. (published 0253 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par 2ND UPDATE: \f28 \uc2 \f2 KOREAN AIR\f28 \uc2 \f2  POSTS NET PROFIT ON \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  GAINS; STRONG 3Q EYED \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Korean Air Lines Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . swung to a net profit in the second quarter as result of foreign-\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  gains, but high fuel costs and a decline in demand for travel to Japan following the March 11 disasters pushed it to an operating loss. (published 0632 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par PTT EXPLORATION TO PAY DIVIDEND OF THB2.61/SHARE FOR 1ST-HALF \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 OPERATIONS\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 PTT Exploration and Production PCL\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Thursday its board approved a plan to pay an interim dividend of THB2.61 per share for its first-half \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . (published 0644 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par DR REDDY'S, FUJIFILM IN PACT TO SET UP JOINT VENTURE FOR GENERIC DRUGS IN JAPAN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 India's \f28 \uc2 \f2 Dr. Reddy's Laboratories\f28 \uc2 \f2  Ltd. and Japan's Fujifilm Corp. Thursday said they have entered into an initial pact to set up a joint venture that will develop generic drugs for the Japanese market. (published 0626 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par FORD CONFIRMS DECISION TO BUILD SECOND CAR FACTORY IN INDIA FOR $900 MLN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Ford Motor Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . Thursday confirmed that it is building a INR40 billion car and engine factory in Gujarat state, and that the plant will start production in 2014. (published 0505 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE:ASIAN SHARES LOWER ON US DEBT CEILING IMPASSE; JAPAN UTILITIES OUTPERFORM \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Asian stock markets were lower Thursday as the U.S. debt ceiling impasse dampened market sentiment, while a stronger yen continued to put pressure on Japanese exporters, though utilities staged a strong rebound after an early sell-off in Tokyo. (published 0452 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ENERGY/COMMODITIES:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: ORIGIN, CONOCO GIVE GREEN LIGHT TO US$20B GAS PROJECT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Origin Energy Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . and \f28 \uc2 \f2 ConocoPhillips\f28 \uc2 \f2  have approved construction of their $20 billion gas export venture in Australia's Queensland state in the latest endorsement of coal seam gas, a nascent form of energy that's never been developed on a large scale. (published 0357 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par MALAYSIA \f28 \uc2 \f2 PETRONAS\f28 \uc2 \f2  MAKES 'SIGNIFICANT' GAS DISCOVERIES OFF SABAH \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Malaysia's state-owned oil company \f28 \uc2 \f2 Petroliam Nasional Bhd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . Thursday said its exploration unit made two "significant" gas discoveries in shallow waters off the west coast of Sabah, with total initial gas-in-place estimated at 1.2 trillion standard cubic feet. (published 0329 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par TAIWAN LOCAL GOVERNMENT DELAYS REVIEW OF NAN YA PLANT RESUMPTIONS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Taiwan's Yunlin county government said Thursday that it has decided to postpone a meeting scheduled for Friday to review an application from \f28 \uc2 \f2 Nan Ya Plastics Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . to reopen three plants at the Mailiao petrochemical complex in Yunlin county that the government ordered shut following fires in May. (published 0624 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par OIL DATA: JAPAN JAN-JUNE CRUDE IMPORTS SLIP; SWEET CRUDE UP \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's crude oil imports in the first half of this year dropped 1.0% from a year earlier despite rising fossil fuel demand to compensate for idle nuclear power capacity, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ministry of Finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said Thursday. (published 0402 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA POWER OUTPUT HITS RECORD HIGH DURING HEAT WAVE -NDRC \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's electricity output for a single day reached a record high on Tuesday due to high temperatures in southern China, according to the National Development and Reform Commission. (published 0335 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA TO RESUME IMPORTS OF CANADA BLACKLEG-INFECTED CANOLA \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China has agreed to resume imports of blackleg-infected Canadian canola, lifting a nearly two-year-old ban, the state-backed China National Grain and Oils Information Center said Thursday. (published 0234 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par NEW ZEALAND GAINS ACCESS TO EU TARIFF-FREE BEEF EXPORT QUOTA \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The European Union has added New Zealand to a group of countries that can annually export a certain amount of grain-fed high-quality beef tariff-free, New Zealand Trade Minister Tim Groser said Thursday. (published 0338 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par IRAQ AKKAS GAS FIELD DEVELOPMENT DEAL LIKELY TO BE FINALIZED IN AUGUST - \f28 \uc2 \f2 KOGAS\f28 \uc2 \f2  OFFICIAL \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Korea Gas Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., or \f28 \uc2 \f2 Kogas\f28 \uc2 \f2 , will likely sign the final contract to develop one of Iraq's largest gas fields in August instead of July as had been previously expected, said an official with the South Korean state-run company Thursday. (published 0059 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par JAPAN'S JANUARY-JUNE LNG IMPORTS UP 8.3% ON YEAR -MOF \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's imports of liquefied natural gas in the January-June period rose 8.3% from a year earlier to 37.6 million metric tons, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ministry of Finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said Thursday. (published 0242 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par AQUILA RESOURCES SAYS 4Q, FY ISAAC PLAINS COAL OUTPUT FELL \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Aquila Resources Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., a junior mining company exploring for iron ore and other minerals in Australia and South Africa, said Thursday that it expects the Isaac Plains coal mine to produce 2.8 million metric tons in the year ahead, after output and sales were crimped by rains and one of several disputes with partner \f28 \uc2 \f2 Vale SA\f28 \uc2 \f2  . (published 0100 GMT) [ 28-07-11 0713GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 62550   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110728e77s000rv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
