\par\par \b \uc2 Dow Jones Asia-Pacific Top Stories Sked For July 26\b0\par\par\uc2 1,939 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Juli 2011\par 09:04\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 Following are the top Asia-Pacific stories featured on Dow Jones Newswires as of 0700 GMT. Not all stories appear on all wires. Please direct any questions or comments to asianewseds@dowjones.com.\par \par \uc2 MACRO/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 /FIXED INCOME:\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: RBI GETS AGGRESSIVE ON INFLATION WITH 50 BP RATE HIKE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 India's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  raised its interest rates by 50 basis points Tuesday, tightening more aggressively than expected in an effort to get a grip on an inflation problem that it warned could grow worse. (published 0646 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par 2ND UPDATE: \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 JAPAN\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  OFFICIALS WATCHFUL OF YEN AMID \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  CALLS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Amid escalating calls from Japanese manufacturers for official action to weaken the yen, Japan's finance minister emphasized Tuesday that he would be vigilant against the rising \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , though his warning failed to stop the yen from touching a fresh four-month high. (published 0637 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par ROUBINI SAYS US WON'T DEFAULT BUT WILL SEE A FISCAL DRAG \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Economist Nouriel Roubini, known for his prescient warnings about the 2008 financial crisis, said Tuesday the U.S. won't default on its debt but the country will suffer a fiscal drag. (published 0634 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par RBA STEVENS CAUTIONS AGAINST TOO MUCH GLOOM ON CONSUMER DEMAND \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 After a long period of building savings and cutting credit card debts, Australia's cautious consumers may not be far from loosening their purse strings, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Reserve Bank of Australia\f28 \uc2 \f2  Governor \f28 \uc2 \f2 Glenn Stevens\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Tuesday. (published 0305 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  MANAGER: PROBLEMATIC TO SPEND \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  RESERVES DOMESTICALLY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The manager of China's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves released a second statement in less than a week disputing claims made by its domestic critics, saying on Tuesday that it would be problematic to use the reserves for domestic purposes as some advocate. (published 0655 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  REGULATOR: END-MARCH TOTAL FOREIGN FINANCIAL ASSETS $4.395 TLN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's total foreign assets came to $4.395 trillion at the end of March, up 7% from the end of 2010, the country's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  management agency said Tuesday. (published 0106 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: CHINA TIGHTENS MONITORING OF FOREIGN FIRMS' YUAN CONVERSIONS - REPORT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China has ordered banks to tighten scrutiny of foreign companies' conversions of foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  into Chinese yuan, the state-run Shanghai Securities News reported Tuesday. (published 0555 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par S KOREA: INFLATION TO REMAIN AT 4% RANGE FOR SOME TIME \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The South Korean government said Tuesday inflation levels will remain around the 4% range for the near future, but vowed to take all necessary measures to meet its 2011 inflation target of 4.0%. (published 0230 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par 2ND UPDATE: S KOREA TO RAISE ELECTRICITY CHARGES, COMPLICATING INFLATION FIGHT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The South Korean government Tuesday said it will raise electricity charges by 4.9% on average from Aug. 1 to help the nation's electricity provider finance its fuel costs. (published 0439 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: NZ SURPLUS NARROWS AS NZ DOLLAR WEIGHS, COMMODITY PRICES FALL \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 New Zealand's trade surplus narrowed in June as an historically high New Zealand dollar and a pull back in commodity prices weighed on exports. (published 0336 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: SINGAPORE JUNE FACTORY OUTPUT REBOUNDS; MAY GAIN TRACTION \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Singapore's manufacturing output rebounded in June, after two straight months of contraction, and analysts expect growth to gain traction in the second half of the year. (published 0544 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: PHILIPPINE IMPORTS GROWTH IN MAY SLOWEST SINCE NOVEMBER 2009 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The value of the Philippines' imports rose 1.6% in May to $4.89 billion from $4.81 billion in the same month last year, the slowest year-on-year growth since November 2009, when imports started to revive after months of contraction, the National Statistics Office said Tuesday. (published 0439 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: INDONESIA'S SHORT-TERM FOREIGN DEBT $49.31 BLN AS OF MAY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Indonesia's short-term foreign debt totaled $49.31 billion at the end of May, amounting to less than a quarter of the country's total offshore debt of $220.15 billion, preliminary data from Bank Indonesia showed Tuesday. (published 0329 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par 2ND UPDATE: INDIAN OIL PRICES $500 MLN 10-YEAR BOND TO YIELD 5.729% - TERM SHEET \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 State-run oil refiner \f28 \uc2 \f2 Indian Oil Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . has priced a $500 million 10-year U.S. dollar bond at 99.217 to yield 5.729%, or 275 basis points over comparable Treasurys, according to a term sheet for the offering seen by Dow Jones Newswires Tuesday. (published 0256 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par HANGZHOU ZHONGCE RUBBER SEEKS TO PAY AROUND 2% YIELD FOR PLANNED YUAN BONDS - TERM SHEET \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Unlisted Chinese tire manufacturer \f28 \uc2 \f2 Hangzhou Zhongce Rubber Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . is seeking to pay around 2% yield on its planned three-year yuan-denominated bonds, according to a term sheet seen by Dow Jones Newswires Tuesday. (published 0259 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par PREVIEW: TAIWAN 2Q GDP GROWTH LIKELY SLOWED TO 4.50% \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Taiwan's economy likely continued expanding in the second quarter from a year earlier due to resilient exports and domestic demand, although growth probably slowed due to a stronger local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  that damped demand for its exports and temporary supply-chain disruptions following the strong earthquake in Japan in March. (published 0643 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par PREVIEW: RBNZ LIKELY TO HOLD OFFICIAL CASH RATE AT 2.5% \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Reserve Bank of New Zealand is expected to hold the Official Cash Rate at 2.50% Thursday, but there are growing murmurs that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will raise the rate in coming months as growth remains strong and inflation high. (published 0442 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 EQUITIES:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par 2ND UPDATE: BAIDU 2ND-QUARTER NET PROFIT NEARLY DOUBLES; STRONG REVENUE GROWTH SEEN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Chinese Internet search giant \f28 \uc2 \f2 Baidu Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Tuesday its second-quarter net profit nearly doubled from a year earlier as it attracted more advertisers and as marketing customers stepped up their spending, and the company gave a better-than-expected revenue forecast for the third quarter. (published 0244 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par 2ND UPDATE: SINGAPORE GIC REDUCES EXPOSURE TO DEVELOPED MARKETS; ASIA GAINS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \uc2 \f2 Government of Singapore Investment Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . has reduced its exposure in developed markets and increased its portfolio in emerging economies, suggesting that the current global uncertainties may continue to weigh on the sovereign wealth fund's investment strategy. (published 0527 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par BHP BILLITON WAITING PERIOD FOR US$12.1 BLN PETROHAWK BID CUT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 BHP Billiton Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 .'s US$12 .1 billion bid for \f28 \uc2 \f2 Petrohawk Energy Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . has had a waiting period cut by the U.S. Federal Trade Commission, the companies said Monday. (published 0016 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par BHP BILLITON RETAINING PETROHAWK EMPLOYEES KEY TO TAKEOVER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 BHP Billiton Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 .'s decision to pursue a US$12.1 billion bid for \f28 \uc2 \f2 Petrohawk Energy Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . hinged in large part on retaining the U.S. company's staff to help the resources giant develop a growing portfolio of shale assets. (published 0118 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: EXXON PROGRESSES PNG EXPANSION PLANS - OIL SEARCH \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Exploration drilling that could support an expansion of \f28 \uc2 \f2 ExxonMobil Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 .'s US$15 billion gas export venture in Papua New Guinea will start before the end of the year, project partner \f28 \uc2 \f2 Oil Search Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Tuesday. (published 0234 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par BUKIT ASAM 1H NET PROFIT IDR1.613 TLN VS IDR901.07 BLN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 PT Bukit Asam said Tuesday its net profit rose to IDR1.613 trillion during the first half of the year from IDR901.07 billion a year earlier on higher revenue. (published 0026 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par SINOHYDRO GROUP PLANS TO SELL UP TO 3.5 BLN SHARES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Sinohydro Group Ltd., China's largest hydropower station builder, said Monday it plans to sell up to 3.5 billion A shares, which are only open to Chinese buyers, ahead of a listing in Shanghai. (published 0032 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par WSJ: NISSAN TO ANNOUNCE CHINA MANUFACTURING EXPANSION - SOURCES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's \f28 \uc2 \f2 Nissan Motor Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . is set to announce a significant expansion of its production capacity in China, including a joint venture plant to produce micro minivans, people with knowledge of the matter said. (published 0248 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par ZIJIN MINING TO RAISE STAKE IN NORTON GOLD BY A$27.67 MLN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Zijin Mining Group Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., China's largest gold producer by output, said Tuesday it will raise its stake in Australia's \f28 \uc2 \f2 Norton Gold Fields\f28 \uc2 \f2  by A$27.67 million, as part of efforts to boost gold reserves. (published 0002 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par KUMHO TO UNLOAD 20M SHARES IN DAEWOO ENGINEERING & CONSTRUCTION \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Kumho Industrial Co. said Tuesday that it has decided to unload its 20 million shares in \f28 \uc2 \f2 Daewoo Engineering & Construction Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . to raise up to KRW273 billion . (published 2322 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CITRA MARGA TO ISSUE 200 MLN RIGHTS SHARES AT IDR1,200 EACH \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Toll road operator and builder PT Citra Marga Nusaphala Persada said Tuesday it plans to issue 200 million non-preemptive rights shares, or 10% of its total equity, at an indicative price of IDR1,200 each. (published 0107 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UTV SOFTWARE: BOARD APPROVES WALT DISNEY PROPOSAL TO DELIST FIRM \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 UTV Software Communications Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . Tuesday said its board approved a proposal from majority shareholder \f28 \uc2 \f2 Walt Disney Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . to buy out other shareholders and delist the firm from Indian exchanges. (published 0332 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA SECURITIES REGULATOR SAYS \f28 \uc2 \f2 ARCELORMITTAL\f28 \uc2 \f2  FAILED TO FULFIL CONTRACTUAL OBLIGATIONS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's securities regulator said \f28 \uc2 \f2 ArcelorMittal\f28 \uc2 \f2  has failed to fulfill its contractual obligations with Hunan Valin Iron & Steel Co., including providing advanced technologies and help in purchasing iron ore, a statement from Hunan Valin showed Tuesday. (published 0426 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UNITED PHOSPHORUS BUYS 51% STAKE IN DVA AGRO BRAZIL \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 India's \f28 \uc2 \f2 United Phosphorus Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Tuesday that it has acquired a 51% stake in \f28 \uc2 \f2 DVA Agro\f28 \uc2 \f2  Brazil from Germany's DVA Group and other shareholders for an undisclosed amount. (published 0337 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par FIRST GEN RAISES PHP10B FROM PREFERRED SHARE PLACEMENT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Philippine power generation firm \f28 \uc2 \f2 First Gen Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Tuesday it has raised PHP10 billion from the private placement of perpetual preferred shares, double the original amount planned because of strong demand. (published 0404 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par HTC: HEAD OF INNOVATION \f28 \uc2 \f2 HORACE LUKE\f28 \uc2 \f2  RESIGNED APRIL 30 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 26-07-11 0704GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 HTC Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 .'s head of innovation, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Horace Luke\f28 \uc2 \f2  resigned on April 30, a company spokesperson said Tuesday. (published 0422 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 AIR NEW ZEALAND\f28 \uc2 \f2  JUNE PASSENGERS RISE ON RIVAL CANCELLATIONS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 National carrier \f28 \uc2 \f2 Air New Zealand Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Tuesday it carried 1.1 million passengers in June, up 2.3% from a year earlier as flight cancellations by other airlines early in the month increased demand for the company's services. (published 0342 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par ZYNGA AND TENCENT LAUNCH ONLINE GAME IN CHINA \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.S. social games star \f28 \uc2 \f2 Zynga\f28 \uc2 \f2  made its debut in Mainland China with a localized "\f28 \uc2 \f2 Zynga\f28 \uc2 \f2  City" title launched in an alliance with leading Chinese Internet service \f28 \uc2 \f2 Tencent Holdings Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . . (published 0342 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: ASIAN SHARES MOSTLY UP; SOLID EARNINGS BOOST TOKYO SHARES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Asian stock markets were mostly higher Tuesday with positive earnings results lifting the Tokyo market, but regional sentiment remained cautious after comments from U.S. President Obama indicated little progress in negotiations to raise the debt ceiling. (published 0440 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ENERGY/COMMODITIES:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par MYANMAR TO CLOSE OIL, GAS EXPLORATION TENDER AUG. 23 -OFFICIAL \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Myanmar will continue taking bids from foreign companies to explore for oil and gas in the interior of the country until Aug. 23, with the tender to stay open 20 days longer than previously announced, a senior government official said Tuesday. (published 0508 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par INDIA FOOD MINISTER: MAY DECIDE ON MORE SUGAR EXPORTS AFTER SEPTEMBER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 India, the world's second-largest sugar producer, may decide on allowing more sugar exports after September, Food Minister K.V. Thomas said Tuesday. (published 0638 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par JAPAN TO BURN RADIATION-TAINTED BEEF \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan announced a plan Tuesday under which beef tainted with radiation from the Fukushima nuclear disaster will be bought up and burnt, in a move aimed at restoring consumer confidence. (published 0420 GMT) [ 26-07-11 0704GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 62550   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110726e77q000jm\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgo