\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Economic Stories Of The Day\b0\par\par\uc2 994 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Juli 2011\par 12:59\par \uc2 Dow Jones Asian Equities Report\par \uc2 AER\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UK ECONOMY EKES OUT MODEST GROWTH IN 2Q \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The U.K's economic growth slowed sharply in the second quarter after the royal wedding and Japanese tsunami dented production, increasing pressure on Chancellor of the Exchequer George Osborne to soften his aggressive austerity program. (published 1112 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UK SERVICES OUTPUT SURGES IN MAY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The U.K.'s dominant industry, the services sector, surged in May as output recovered from a markedly weak month in April, official figures showed Tuesday. (published 1033 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par GREECE TO PROCEED WITH BOND SWAP DEAL IN AUGUST -DEP FIN MIN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Greece expects to implement a deal with private creditors to swap their holdings of Greek bonds with longer-dated securities next month, the country's deputy finance minister said in a television interview Tuesday. (published 1043 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par FRENCH CONSUMER CONFIDENCE POINTS TO SPENDING REBOUND \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 French consumer confidence rose unexpectedly in July, data showed Tuesday, pointing to a rebound in spending after recent data has shown consumers are dragging on growth in the euro zone's second largest economy. (published 1111 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par SPANISH, ITALIAN SHORT-TERM BORROWING COSTS SOAR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Spain and Italy once again paid sharply higher yields than a month ago to sell short-term debt Tuesday, indicating that euro-zone bond markets remain fragile despite last Thursday's Greek bailout agreement. (published 1138 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par CHINA \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  REGULATOR: END-MARCH TOTAL FOREIGN FINANCIAL ASSETS $4.395 TLN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's total foreign assets came to $4.395 trillion at the end of March, up 7% from the end of 2010, the country's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  management agency said Tuesday. (published 0106 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par CHINA TIGHTENS MONITORING OF FOREIGN FIRMS' YUAN CONVERSIONS - REPORT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China has ordered banks to tighten scrutiny of foreign companies' conversions of foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  into Chinese yuan, the state-run Shanghai Securities News reported Tuesday. (published 0555 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par JAPAN ECONOMY MINISTER VOICES CONCERN ABOUT STRONG YEN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's economy minister Kaoru Yosano said Tuesday that sudden, excessive surges in the yen have negative consequences for the country's economy, in the latest sign of concern over the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's recent rises. (published 0136 GMT)\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 JAPAN\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  FINANCE MINISTER WATCHFUL OF YEN AMID \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  CALLS \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's finance minister emphasized his vigilance against the rising yen Tuesday, as Japanese manufacturers escalated their calls for official action to weaken the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , but the warnings didn't keep the yen from touching a fresh four-month high. (published 0231 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par GERMAN GFK AUG CONSUMER SENTIMENT AT 5.4 VS 5.5 IN JULY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 German market research group GfK's forward-looking consumer climate index is set to decline in August, as discussions about the exit strategy from the Greek debt crisis damped consumer sentiment, Reuters news agency said Tuesday. (published 0700 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par INDIA PM ADVISOR: \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CENTRAL BANK\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  TO REVERSE POLICY STANCE ONLY IF INFLATION DEFINITELY TRENDS DOWN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \uc2 \f2 Reserve Bank of India\f28 \uc2 \f2  will stop raising rates only when inflation shows definite signs of trending down, the Prime Minister's Economic Advisory Council Chairman C. Rangarajan said Tuesday. (published 0825 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par FITCH: INDIA'S TIGHT MONETARY POLICY IS APPROPRIATE RESPONSE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Higher interest rates in India will hurt short-term economic activity, but they are unlikely to have any impact on long-term growth potential, a director at Fitch Ratings said Tuesday. (published 0830 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par S KOREA: INFLATION TO REMAIN AT 4% RANGE FOR SOME TIME \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The South Korean government said Tuesday inflation levels will remain around the 4% range for the near future, but vowed to take all necessary measures to meet its 2011 inflation target of 4.0%. (published 0230 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par RBA STEVENS CAUTIONS AGAINST TOO MUCH GLOOM ON CONSUMER DEMAND \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 After a long period of building savings and cutting credit card debts, Australia's cautious consumers may not be far from loosening their purse strings, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Reserve Bank of Australia\f28 \uc2 \f2  Governor \f28 \uc2 \f2 Glenn Stevens\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Tuesday. (published 0305 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par OBAMA, BOEHNER TAKE DEFICIT PLANS TO US CITIZENS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 With the nation at risk for a default on its debt just over a week away, President Barack Obama and House Speaker John Boehner pitched their divergent plans for solving the nation's fiscal problems directly to American citizens. (published 0207 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par BANK OF FRANCE: NOYER DID NOT USE "STRONG VIGILANCE" CODE WORD \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Bank of France governor Christian Noyer in a newspaper interview did not use the sensitive "strong vigilance" code word that is generally understood to signal an imminent interest rate increase, the French \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said Tuesday. (published 1128 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par GREEK FINANCE MINISTER: PRESSURE EASED WITH NEW FINANCING DEAL \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A new European and private sector financing package bought Greece critical reprieve from its oppressive debt burden, giving the beleaguered economy fresh momentum for growth, Greece's finance minister said Monday. (published 0056 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par     ======= DOW JONES NEWSWIRES ANALYSIS AND COMMENTARY ======= \par  \par EUROPEAN INTEREST RATE TECHNICALS: TO TEST KEY RESISTANCE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Intraday BUND: The recovery is beginning to show signs of struggling in front of key resistance at 128.61. Monday's cap at 128.45 is also part of the close-knit resistance cluster, and given Monday's unimpressive volume a break higher through 128.61 towards 128.84 can only be achieved on a fresh wave of bull pressure. Failure to break through 128.61, combined with a break below 127.64, would prompt a setback towards 127.24 and 126.90. (published 0708 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par EUROPEAN \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  TECHNICALS: ACROSS-BOARD USD WEAKNESS DOMINATES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Intraday EUR/USD: The 1.4500 level is being challenged, as scope has been created for 1.4580. Tuesday's Asian session break above 1.4395 completes a two-day consolidation phase, and a seven-week bear resistance line near 1.4500 is likely to be broken. EUR bulls are still on course for meeting the 1.618 extension target at 1.4733 in the longer-term. Corrective weakness will attract support while above 1.4406 and only below 1.4391 would question the bullish EUR outlook. (published 0722 GMT) [ 26-07-11 1059GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1030 1804 4180   \par \par \uc2 Dokument AER0000020110726e77q0000w\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
