e-run Shanghai Securities News reported Tuesday. (published 0555 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par JAPAN ECONOMY MINISTER VOICES CONCERN ABOUT STRONG YEN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's economy minister Kaoru Yosano said Tuesday that sudden, excessive surges in the yen have negative consequences for the country's economy, in the latest sign of concern over the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's recent rises. (published 0136 GMT)\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 JAPAN\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  FINANCE MINISTER WATCHFUL OF YEN AMID \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  CALLS \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's finance minister emphasized his vigilance against the rising yen Tuesday, as Japanese manufacturers escalated their calls for official action to weaken the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , but the warnings didn't keep the yen from touching a fresh four-month high. (published 0231 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par GERMAN GFK AUG CONSUMER SENTIMENT AT 5.4 VS 5.5 IN JULY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 German market research group GfK's forward-looking consumer climate index is set to decline in August, as discussions about the exit strategy from the Greek debt crisis damped consumer sentiment, Reuters news agency said Tuesday. (published 0700 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par INDIA PM ADVISOR: \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CENTRAL BANK\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  TO REVERSE POLICY STANCE ONLY IF INFLATION DEFINITELY TRENDS DOWN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \uc2 \f2 Reserve Bank of India\f28 \uc2 \f2  will stop raising rates only when inflation shows definite signs of trending down, the Prime Minister's Economic Advisory Council Chairman C. Rangarajan said Tuesday. (published 0825 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par FITCH: INDIA'S TIGHT MONETARY POLICY IS APPROPRIATE RESPONSE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Higher interest rates in India will hurt short-term economic activity, but they are unlikely to have any impact on long-term growth potential, a director at Fitch Ratings said Tuesday. (published 0830 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par S KOREA: INFLATION TO REMAIN AT 4% RANGE FOR SOME TIME \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The South Korean government said Tuesday inflation levels will remain around the 4% range for the near future, but vowed to take all necessary measures to meet its 2011 inflation target of 4.0%. (published 0230 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par S KOREA TO RAISE ELECTRICITY CHARGES, COMPLICATING INFLATION FIGHT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The South Korean government Tuesday said it will raise electricity charges by 4.9% on average from Aug. 1 to help the nation's electricity provider finance its fuel costs. (published 0439 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par RBA STEVENS CAUTIONS AGAINST TOO MUCH GLOOM ON CONSUMER DEMAND \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 After a long period of building savings and cutting credit card debts, Australia's cautious consumers may not be far from loosening their purse strings, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Reserve Bank of Australia\f28 \uc2 \f2  Governor \f28 \uc2 \f2 Glenn Stevens\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Tuesday. (published 0305 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UPDATE:NZ SURPLUS NARROWS AS NZ DOLLAR WEIGHS, COMMODITY PRICES FALL \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 New Zealand's trade surplus narrowed in June as an historically high New Zealand dollar and a pull back in commodity prices weighed on exports. (published 0336 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par OBAMA, BOEHNER TAKE DEFICIT PLANS TO US CITIZENS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 With the nation at risk for a default on its debt just over a week away, President Barack Obama and House Speaker John Boehner pitched their divergent plans for solving the nation's fiscal problems directly to American citizens. (published 0207 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par ECB'S NOYER: STRONG VIGILANCE OVER CPI - REPORT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's stance remains one of strong vigilance over inflation, ECB governing council member Christian Noyer says in an interview Tuesday, reiterating the ECB's stance of never pre-committing on monetary policy. (published 0817 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par GREEK FINANCE MINISTER: PRESSURE EASED WITH NEW FINANCING DEAL \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A new European and private sector financing package bought Greece critical reprieve from its oppressive debt burden, giving the beleaguered economy fresh momentum for growth, Greece's finance minister said Monday. (published 0056 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par     ======= DOW JONES NEWSWIRES ANALYSIS AND COMMENTARY ======= \par  \par EUROPEAN INTEREST RATE TECHNICALS: TO TEST KEY RESISTANCE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Intraday BUND: The recovery is beginning to show signs of struggling in front of key resistance at 128.61. Monday's cap at 128.45 is also part of the close-knit resistance cluster, and given Monday's unimpressive volume a break higher through 128.61 towards 128.84 can only be achieved on a fresh wave of bull pressure. Failure to break through 128.61, combined with a break below 127.64, would prompt a setback towards 127.24 and 126.90. (published 0708 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par EUROPEAN \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  TECHNICALS: ACROSS-BOARD USD WEAKNESS DOMINATES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Intraday EUR/USD: The 1.4500 level is being challenged, as scope has been created for 1.4580. Tuesday's Asian session break above 1.4395 completes a two-day consolidation phase, and a seven-week bear resistance line near 1.4500 is likely to be broken. EUR bulls are still on course for meeting the 1.618 extension target at 1.4733 in the longer-term. Corrective weakness will attract support while above 1.4406 and only below 1.4391 would question the bullish EUR outlook. (published 0722 GMT) [ 26-07-11 1002GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1030 1804 4180   \par \par \uc2 Dokument AER0000020110726e77q0000v\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
