n from touching a fresh four-month high. (published 0231 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par GERMAN GFK AUG CONSUMER SENTIMENT AT 5.4 VS 5.5 IN JULY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 German market research group GfK's forward-looking consumer climate index is set to decline in August, as discussions about the exit strategy from the Greek debt crisis damped consumer sentiment, Reuters news agency said Tuesday. (published 0700 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par INDIA PM ADVISOR: \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CENTRAL BANK\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  TO REVERSE POLICY STANCE ONLY IF INFLATION DEFINITELY TRENDS DOWN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \uc2 \f2 Reserve Bank of India\f28 \uc2 \f2  will stop raising rates only when inflation shows definite signs of trending down, the Prime Minister's Economic Advisory Council Chairman C. Rangarajan said Tuesday. (published 0825 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par FITCH: INDIA'S TIGHT MONETARY POLICY IS APPROPRIATE RESPONSE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Higher interest rates in India will hurt short-term economic activity, but they are unlikely to have any impact on long-term growth potential, a director at Fitch Ratings said Tuesday. (published 0830 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par S KOREA: INFLATION TO REMAIN AT 4% RANGE FOR SOME TIME \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The South Korean government said Tuesday inflation levels will remain around the 4% range for the near future, but vowed to take all necessary measures to meet its 2011 inflation target of 4.0%. (published 0230 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par S KOREA TO RAISE ELECTRICITY CHARGES, COMPLICATING INFLATION FIGHT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The South Korean government Tuesday said it will raise electricity charges by 4.9% on average from Aug. 1 to help the nation's electricity provider finance its fuel costs. (published 0439 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par RBA STEVENS CAUTIONS AGAINST TOO MUCH GLOOM ON CONSUMER DEMAND \f28 \par \par