\par\par \b \uc2 WORLD  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 : Markets Glad About Greece, Worried About Washington\b0\par\par\uc2 535 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Juli 2011\par 03:08\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 -- Euro remains strong as market digests news of Greek bailout program\par \par \uc2 -- Attention now on U.S. debt ceiling standoff\par \par \uc2 -- Yen pulls back from highest since March G-7 \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    By William Sposato \par    Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 TOKYO (Dow Jones)--The euro held most of its overnight gains on news of a comprehensive bailout package for Greece that also lays the groundwork for stronger governance in the euro zone, as market concerns shifted to the debt showdown in Washington.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The EUR159 billion Greek bailout, with official loans and private-sector participation, "went beyond market expectations," \f28 \uc2 \f2 BNP Paribas\f28 \uc2 \f2  said in a research note, calling the agreement "a major step towards stabilizing the markets and a resolution of the debt crisis."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Leaders of the 17 euo members also agreed on a broader framework for countries including Ireland and Portugal, as well as enhancing the European Financial Stability Facility, giving the bailout fund more flexibility in its purchases and allowing it to buy sovereign debt in the secondary market if deemed necessary.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The rescue's "key development" is that the European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  can still accept Greek bonds as collateral for refinancing \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  even if ratings agencies deem Greece to be in "selective default," said economist Daisuke Karakama at \f28 \uc2 \f2 Mizuho Corporate Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The euro jumped to $1.4440 in late U.S. afternoon trade. As Asia opened, the common \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  moved off its highs; at 0108 GMT it was at $1.4391. The euro climbed to Y113.29 before pulling back to Y113.21 by mid-morning, vs Y112.98 late in New York.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The dollar was weaker as the countdown continued on the showdown between the White House and congressional Republicans over raising the U.S. debt ceiling and avoiding a downgrade for U.S. Treasurys. The U.S. will reach its borrowing limit Aug. 2; debate is focused on how to attach a long-term deficit-reduction plan to any increase in the debt ceiling.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 But the yen pulled back from its highs against the U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . Japanese Finance Minister Yoshihiko Noda again Friday called the yen moves "one sided," but traders are skeptical about the possibility of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  as officials repeatedly say the problems is more about a weak dollar than a strong yen.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The dollar fell in late U.S. trade to Y78.22, its weakest since just before the March 18 \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the Group of Seven that followed \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's earthquake and tsunami. It was later at Y78.65.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Tokyo shares are taking the strong yen in stride, with the Nikkei Stock Average staying around 10,000.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "It's hard to expect Japanese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  unless we see a clear negative impact to the Japanese economy, say, a plunge in stocks," said Osamu Takashima, Citibank Japan chief \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The pound was at $1.6312 vs $1.6315 late in New York. The dollar was at CHF0.8175 from CHF0.8150. The ICE Dollar Index was at 74.000 from 73.910.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By William Sposato, Dow Jones Newswires; 81-3-6269-2785; william.sposato@dowjones.com\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -Kosaku Narioka and Takashi Mochizuki contributed to this story. [ 22-07-11 0108GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1034 1863 28038 4162   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110722e77m00020\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
