rly chart); breach would expose upside to 80.38 (July 12 high), then 80.83 (July 11 high), 81.33 (100-day moving average) and 81.49 (July 8 high). Support at 78.82 (yesterday's low), then at 78.45 (Thursday's low, matching 76.4% Fibonacci retracement of advance from March 17 record low of 76.25 to April 6 high of 85.53); breach would reinstate near-term negative bias, exposing downside to 76.25, then psychological round-numbered levels of 76.00 and 75.00.\par \par \uc2 -0-\par \par \uc2 Copyright (c) 2011 \uc2 Dow Jones & Company, Inc\uc2 . \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJCFWE0020110721e77k001qr\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
