\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE: Japan Officials Fuss Over Strong Yen, But Imminent Action Unlikely\b0\par\par\uc2 503 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Juli 2011\par 07:18\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 --Japan's finance minister reiterates that recent \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market movements are "one-sided"\par \par \uc2 --BOJ Deputy Governor says bank ready to take action if strong yen damages exports\par \par \uc2 --Finance minister declines to comment on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 (Recasts, adds analyst comments in paragraph 8 and background.)\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    By Tatsuo Ito and Megumi Fujikawa \par    Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 TOKYO (Dow Jones)--Japanese authorities made a lot of noise about the yen's recent strength on Tuesday, but their clamor was phrased in a way that suggests more bark than bite.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Speaking at a parliamentary committee, Finance Minister Yoshihiko Noda reiterated his description of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's recent movement in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market as being "one-sided." He declined to comment on its levels or on the prospects of an \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Recent movement has been one-sided and we will watch developments closely," Noda said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Speaking in the same committee, one of the Bank of Japan's deputy governors said that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  stands ready to take action if the yen's appreciation starts to seriously damage Japan's exports, as well as corporate profits and sentiment.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Deputy Gov. Hirohide Yamaguchi also expressed concern about the possibility that Japanese companies may shift their production overseas and that Japan's long-term growth potential may be consequently lowered by the strong yen.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Having heard these comments a number of times in recent days, analysts said the comments had little impact on the market as participants say the focus is now on the European sovereign debt crisis.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "The caution over \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's potential \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  doesn't seem strong in the market," said Daisuke Karakama, market economist at \f28 \uc2 \f2 Mizuho Corporate Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2 , adding that participants are now awaiting Thursday's meeting of euro-zone leaders on the issue of a new funding package for Greece.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The dollar was hovering around the Y79 line when Noda and Yamaguchi spoke, after hitting Y78.97 Tuesday morning. It was standing at around Y79.06 yen as of 0505 GMT.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Tokyo has stepped up its rhetoric over the strong yen, with Noda saying last week that the dollar's recent drop below Y79.00 "is far out line with real fundamentals and is one-sided."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The verbal warning shows that Japanese officials may be bothered not only by the speed of the yen's appreciation but also its levels.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 But many investors seem to think that sharper yen rises would be needed to trigger Japanese action and that even if Tokyo acts, it would be difficult to reverse the yen's rise, which is being driven by factors beyond Japan's control.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In an interview with Dow Jones Newswires last week, Noda said official action should be limited to when there is "excessive volatility" or "disorderly movement" in the yen's exchange rates.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 --Koasaku Narioka contributed to this story\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Tatsuo Ito and Megumi Fujikawa, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-6269-2786; tatsuo.ito@dowjones.com [ 19-07-11 0518GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110719e77j0008y\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
