\par\par \b \uc2 Dow Jones Asia-Pacific Top Stories Sked For July 14\b0\par\par\uc2 2,223 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Juli 2011\par 09:19\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 Following are the top Asia-Pacific stories featured on Dow Jones Newswires as of 0700 GMT. Not all stories appear on all wires. Please direct any questions or comments to asianewseds@dowjones.com.\par \par \uc2 MACRO/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 /FIXED INCOME:\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par 3RD UPDATE: BOK HOLDS RATE STEADY; TO RESUME HIKES AT MEASURED PACE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Bank of Korea, as expected, held its benchmark interest rate steady at 3.25% Thursday, judging that fresh anxiety over Europe's debt crisis and signs of moderation in inflation pressure give it time to pause after raising the rate last month for the third time this year. (published 0658 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: JAPAN FINANCE MINISTER STEPS UP RHETORIC VS YEN STRENGTH \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's finance minister escalated his warnings against the yen's strength Thursday, calling the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's recent climb "far out of line with real fundamentals," but he kept quiet on the prospect of government \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market. (published 0051 GMT)\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 JAPAN\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  MOF OFFICIAL: GOVT COULD \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENE\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  IN \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  WITHOUT "DECISIVE STEPS" WARNING \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "It is wrong to think we will not \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  unless we say we'll take 'decisive steps,'" the official told reporters. (published 0618 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par 2ND UPDATE: SINGAPORE 2Q GDP SHRINKS MORE THAN EXPECTED BUT 2011 OUTLOOK MAY BE INTACT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Singapore's economy contracted more than expected in the second quarter as Japan's disasters disrupted manufacturers' supply chains, but many economists say the slowdown is temporary and the outlook for the full year may remain unchanged. (published 0255 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par 2ND UPDATE: STRONG NZ 1Q GDP ADVANCES RATE-HIKE EXPECTATIONS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 New Zealand's first-quarter gross domestic product came in well above expectations Thursday, lifting the New Zealand dollar to a post-float high and advancing expectations of a Reserve Bank of New Zealand rate hike. (published 0501 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par S&P: DON'T SEE BIG CHINA BANKS TAKING FULL-YEAR LOSSES FROM LOCAL GOVERNMENT DEBT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Non-performing loans at Chinese local government financing platforms are likely to climb, but that shouldn't cause full-year losses at major banks, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Standard & Poor's\f28 \uc2 \f2  Ratings Services said Thursday. (published 0408 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par FITCH ANALYST: CHINA FOREIGN-\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCY\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  RATING 'WELL SUPPORTED' \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's foreign-\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rating remains "well supported," but it's hard to foresee how Beijing will strike a balance between supporting growth and tackling inflation, a senior analyst at Fitch Ratings has said. (published 0606 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: CHINA MUST ASSESS RISKS AS US DEBT INVESTOR - RESEARCHER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China must assess the risks it faces as a major investor in U.S. Treasurys, and could adjust its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  assets to reduce that risk, a senior Chinese government researcher said Thursday, after Moody's Investors Service warned it was reviewing U.S. Treasurys for a possible credit rating downgrade. (published 0518 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: CHINA DAGONG RATING AGENCY PUTS US ON NEGATIVE WATCH \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Chinese rating agency Dagong Global Credit Rating Co. said Thursday it is putting U.S. sovereign debt on negative watch for a possible downgrade, in a move that echoes Moody's Investors Service's latest warning on the U.S. (published 0325 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par TAIWAN \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CENTRAL BANK\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VIEWS SAFETY, LIQUIDITY KEY IN MANAGING \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  RESERVES - SOURCE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Taiwan's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  remains committed to the view that safety and liquidity are key in managing its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves, an official from the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said Thursday. (published 0710 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par DATA SNAP: INDIA JUNE WHOLESALE PRICE INDEX UP 9.44% ON YEAR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 India's inflation accelerated to 9.44% in June from a provisional reading of 9.06% in the previous month, the government said Thursday. (published 0645 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par DATA SNAP: INDIA PRIMARY ARTICLES WPI DOWN 0.1% IN WEEK TO JULY 2 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The wholesale price index for primary articles in India fell 0.1% to 197.6 in the week ended July 2 from a provisional 197.8 in the previous week, according to data issued Thursday by the Ministry of Commerce and Industry. (published 0625 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par INDIA CHIEF ECONOMIC ADVISER: INFLATION LIKELY A TAD ABOVE 6% BY MARCH \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 India's wholesale price index-based inflation rate may ease to a little above 6% by March 2012, but food price rise readings may stay high in the January-March period because of a weaker base, Chief Economic Adviser Kaushik Basu said Thursday. (published 0520 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA COMMERCE MINISTER: CHINA CONCERNED OVER EU'S TRADE REMEDIES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Chinese Commerce Minister Chen Deming said Thursday that China is deeply concerned over the European Union's trade remedies, especially the latter's anti-subsidy measures. (published 0637 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: NEW ZEALAND, AUSTRALIA MUST STAND TOGETHER, SAYS AUSTRALIAN TREASURER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australian Treasurer Wayne Swan Thursday underscored the importance of creating a Single Economic Market between Australia and New Zealand, in particular given the current global economic backdrop. (published 0533 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par BANK INDONESIA DEPUTY GOVERNOR SEES EASING PRICE RISKS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Bank Indonesia Deputy Gov. Hartadi Sarwono said Thursday headline inflation may reach 4.9% this year, assuming the country's subsidized fuel policy stays unchanged. (published 0359 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par INTERVIEW: MOODY'S: TAIWAN BANKS RESILIENT DESPITE CORPORATE DEFAULT SCARE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Taiwan's banks have sufficient capital to withstand "one to two" corporate loan defaults, an analyst at \f28 \uc2 \f2 Moody's\f28 \uc2 \f2  Investors Services told Dow Jones Newswires in a recent interview. (published 0434 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: THAI CONSUMER CONFIDENCE AT 4-YEAR HIGH; SEEN TRENDING HIGHER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Consumer confidence in Thailand surged to its highest level in four years in June due to expectations that the recent general election results will bring political stability. (published 0512 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: 5-YEAR JGBS MEET SOLID DEMAND AS INVESTORS SEEK SAFE HAVEN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Five-year Japanese government bonds drew strong investor demand at Thursday's auction, confirming popularity of safe-haven assets as the global economic outlook clouds over. (published 0513 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par INDONESIA AIMS TO RAISE IDR7 TLN VIA BOND AUCTION JULY 19 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Indonesia aims to raise IDR7 trillion via a bond auction on July 19 to help plug its budget deficit, the finance ministry said Thursday. (published 0437 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par MCC HOLDING PLANS BENCHMARK FIVE-YEAR DOLLAR BOND - SOURCE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 MCC Holding Corporation Limited, a subsidiary of \f28 \uc2 \f2 China Metallurgical Group Corporation\f28 \uc2 \f2 , is planning to sell an inaugural benchmark five-year dollar bond, a person familiar with the proposed deal said Thursday. (published 0313 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par 6 ANALYSTS POLLED SAY BOK TO HOLD POLICY RATE IN AUGUST - DJ SURVEY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Bank of Korea will likely keep its policy rate steady at 3.25% in August amid heightened global economic uncertainties, six of 11 economists and analysts polled by Dow Jones Newswires said Thursday. (published 0546 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 EQUITIES:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: PEABODY, \f28 \uc2 \f2 ARCELORMITTAL\f28 \uc2 \f2  RAISE OFFER FOR AUSTRALIA'S MACARTHUR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The world's largest listed coal miner and steelmaker on Thursday sweetened their offer for Australian pulverized coal miner \f28 \uc2 \f2 Macarthur Coal Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . to around A$4.73 billion, while moving a step closer to success by agreeing to start due diligence on the deal. (published 0612 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par PIKE RIVER BIDDERS SHORT LISTED, AUGUST SALE UNLIKELY -PRICEWATERHOUSECOOPERS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 PricewaterhouseCoopers LLP\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Wednesday that it has drawn up a short-list of bidders for the assets of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Pike River Coal Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., adding that regulatory issues will likely delay the New Zealand company's sale. (published 0513 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par WSJ: \f28 \uc2 \f2 SAMSUNG ELECTRONICS\f28 \uc2 \f2  SAYS IT WILL CONSIDER RELEASING FULL RESULTS OF CONSULTANT STUDY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Samsung Electronics Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., trying to quell a controversy over cancer-related deaths of workers at its semiconductor complex in suburban Seoul, on Thursday announced results of a study it commissioned by a U.S. environmental consulting firm that concluded its factories were safe. (published 0710 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par DAVID JONES CEO SEES NO SIGNS OF IMPROVING CONSUMER SENTIMENT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 David Jones Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . Chief Executive \f28 \uc2 \f2 Paul Zahra\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Thursday he sees no signs of improving consumer sentiment, after the company issued a profit warning overnight. (published 0218 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 CAPITACOMMERCIAL TRUST\f28 \uc2 \f2 : 2Q DPU 1.92 SINGAPORE CENTS VS 1.97 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 CapitaCommercial Trust Thursday reported a second-quarter distribution per unit of 1.92 Singapore cents, down from 1.97 Singapore cents a year earlier. (published 2313 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par ICBC: EUROPE UNIT 1ST-HALF PROFIT NEARLY US$10 MLN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Industrial & Commercial Bank of China\f28 \uc2 \f2  Ltd. said Thursday its Europe unit had a first-half profit of nearly US$10 million, driven by rises in trade finance and fee income. (published 0355 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par DAEWOO ENGINEERING SIGNS INITIAL DEAL TO BUILD OMAN POWER PLANT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Daewoo Engineering & Construction Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Thursday that it has signed an initial deal to start building a combined-cycle power plant for Phoenix Power Co. SAOC in Oman, with the final contract has yet to be signed later. (published 0253 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par EVA, \f28 \uc2 \f2 CHINA AIRLINES\f28 \uc2 \f2  CUT AIRFARES TO BEIJING, SHANGHAI \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China Airlines and \f28 \uc2 \f2 EVA Airways\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Thursday they have cut airfares for routes to Beijing and Shanghai, which prompted their share prices to fall. (published 0437 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par AECOM WINS ENGINEERING, DESIGN TENDER FOR SYDNEY RAIL WORKS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australia's New South Wales state government said Thursday it awarded an engineering and design tender for a new Sydney railway line to the Australian unit of global services provider \f28 \uc2 \f2 AECOM Technology Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . . (published 0044 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: POSCO TO INVEST C$181M IN CANADA COAL MINE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korean steelmaker Posco said Thursday that it will invest a total of C$181 million in the Mt. Klappan coal mine in Canada via a joint venture it will set up with \f28 \uc2 \f2 Fortune Minerals Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . . (published 0312 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par JAPAN'S NISSHIN STEEL, NIPPON METAL DENY MERGER REPORTS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Nisshin Steel Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Nippon Metal Industry Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . separately denied Thursday that they have agreed to merge their \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . (published 0234 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par PHILIPPINE BOURSE TO EXTEND TRADING FROM OCTOBER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Philippine Stock Exchange said Thursday it will extend trading hours from October this year and then introduce an afternoon session in 2012. (published 0222 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par SEVEN WEST MEDIA SAYS NO PLANS TO BUY MORE RADIO STATIONS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 14-07-11 0719GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Seven West Media Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . rejected Thursday a newspaper report that it was considering buying radio stations. (published 0239 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par EOC: LOOKING AT LISTING ON A STOCK EXCHANGE IN ASIA \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Oslo-listed EOC Ltd. said Thursday it is looking to list on a stock exchange in Asia in a bid to tap new capital markets and expand its presence in the region. (published 0627 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: ASIAN SHARES MIXED, DOLLAR SLIDES; TOKYO EXPORTERS FALTER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Asian stock markets were mixed Thursday, with sentiment hurt as the U.S. dollar fell broadly after Moody's Investors Service warned of a possible downgrade of U.S. government debt, pushing gold plays higher and hurting many exporters' stocks in Tokyo. (published 0502 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ENERGY/COMMODITIES:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par JAPAN TO PERFORM FINAL CHECKS ON TWO NUCLEAR REACTORS, MAY RETURN TO FULL SERVICE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japanese officials are set to perform final checks on two nuclear reactors that are currently undergoing test-runs, which would make them the first reactors to get the green light to return to full service after the March 11 earthquake and tsunami sparked the country's worst-ever nuclear crisis. (published 0622 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA'S MOVES TO INCREASE HOG NUMBERS MAY TAKE MONTHS -ANALYSTS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Government measures to raise China's hog population to head off sharp pork price rises may produce only limited results in the second half of the year, trimming the extent to which Beijing hopes to restrain prices after reaching record levels in mid-June, analysts said Thursday. (published 0417 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: INDONESIA MAY BAN SUBSIDIZED FUELS FOR PRIVATE CARS AFTER AUGUST - OFFICIAL \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Indonesian government may go ahead with a plan to ban the use of subsidized fuels in private cars after August to limit the costs of fuel subsidies, Oil and Gas Director-General Evita Legowo said Thursday. (published 0445 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par JAPAN GOVT EDANO: PM DIDN'T SAY JAPAN WILL PHASE OUT NUCLEAR ENERGY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's top government spokesman said Thursday that remarks by Prime Minister Naoto Kan yesterday did not indicate that Japan would eliminate the use of nuclear energy. (published 0249 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CNOOC: CONTINUE TO ASSIST \f28 \uc2 \f2 CONOCOPHILLIPS\f28 \uc2 \f2  TO COMPLETE BOHAI BAY CLEANUP \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Cnooc Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Wednesday that it will continue assisting \f28 \uc2 \f2 ConocoPhillips\f28 \uc2 \f2  to clean up oil leaks in northeastern China's Bohai Bay after the government ordered its partner to halt production at two offshore oil platforms. (published 0028 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par INDONESIA AWARDS TWO COAL-BED METHANE BLOCKS -OFFICIAL \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Indonesia Thursday awarded two coal-bed methane blocks to investors, from a total of seven blocks it offered for bids earlier this year, a government official said. (published 0153 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: FONTERRA CO-OPERATIVE GROUP APPOINTS THEO SPIERINGS AS CEO, EFFECTIVE SEP 26 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The appointment of Dutchman Theo Spierings as the new chief executive of New Zealand milk giant Fonterra Co-Operative Group Ltd. was widely welcomed Wednesday, with the 46-year-old's wealth of experience in the industry garnering him support. (published 0351 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: ILUKA RAISES 2011 PRODUCTION, COST GUIDANCE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 --Iluka Is The World's Largest Producer Of Zircon. (published 0009 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par AUSTRALIAN TRANSGENIC WHEAT TRIALS STOPPED BY GREENPEACE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Two environmental activists from Greenpeace Thursday smashed experimental trials of genetically modified wheat being conducted by Australia's premier science agency, the Commonwealth Scientific and Industrial Research Organization, Greenpeace said. (published 2331 GMT Wednesday)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par AUSTRALIA MOVES TO UPGRADE ANIMAL WELFARE OF LIVE SHEEP TRADE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australian government officials and sheep-export industry representatives will work to raise animal welfare for the lucrative trade to international standards, Agriculture Minister Joe Ludwig said late Wednesday. (published 0148 GMT) [ 14-07-11 0719GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 62550   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110714e77e000jk\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
