\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Options:Dollar/Yen Options Up Amid  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Concern\b0\par\par\uc2 391 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Juli 2011\par 05:39\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 TOKYO (Dow Jones)--Speculation that the dollar may slide further against the yen, after Federal Reserve Chairman Ben Bernanke said Wednesday the Fed may undertake a new round of easing, fueled demand for \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  options to hedge against further dollar-yen falls and the yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  they could bring.\par \par \uc2 One-month at-the-money dollar/yen volatilities rose to 10.20%/10.90% from 9.55%/10.25% late Wednesday in New York, as options dealers said further rises could be in store in coming sessions.\par \par \uc2 One market participant bought a one-month at-the-money straddle option contract with implied volatility at 10.50% and a face value of around $50 million, an options dealer at a major Japanese bank said. The contract profits on any wide swings in the underlying exchange rate.\par \par \uc2 Highlighting concerns that any sharper falls in the spot market could prompt \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  to order up yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , one player bought a two-week dollar-call/yen-put options contract with a strike price of Y80.00, implied volatility of 10.80% and a face value of around $100 million, the dealer said.\par \par \uc2 As the contract profits if the dollar is trading above Y80.00 at the time of its expiry, the player could be banking on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  or speculation of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  buoying the greenback back above that level in coming sessions.\par \par \uc2 The dollar fell to a fresh four-month low of Y78.45 earlier in the day.\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    1-Month Option Implied Volatilities At 0300 GMT \par  \par               Tokyo           New York        Tokyo \par               Thursday        Wednesday       Wednesday \par Dollar/Yen    10.20%/10.90%   9.55%/10.25%    9.90%/10.60% \par Euro/Dollar   12.95%/13.20%   12.95%/13.20%   13.85%/14.10% \par Euro/Yen      14.05%/15.05%   14.15%/15.15%   14.45%/15.45% \par  \par  \par    3-Month Option Implied Volatilities \par  \par               Tokyo          Tokyo \par               Thursday       Wednesday \par Dollar/Yen    10.20%/10.80%  10.10%/10.70% \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The volatilities used are over-the-counter, at-the-money rates.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1-month 25 delta risk-reversals favor dollar put/yen call options by 0.95%/1.45% compared with 0.70%/1.20% in Tokyo Wednesday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Andrew Monahan, Dow Jones Newswires; 81-3-6269-2783; andrew.monahan@dowjones.com [ 14-07-11 0339GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1077 4127   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110714e77e0007i\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
