\par\par \b \uc2 WORLD  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 : Euro Gains After \uc2 Moody's\uc2  Warning, Bernanke Comments\b0\par\par\uc2 811 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Juli 2011\par 03:34\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 -- Dollar falls against euro and yen after \uc2 Moody's\uc2  puts U.S. debt on review for possible downgrade\par \par \uc2 -- U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  also hit by dovish comments from Fed Chairman Bernanke\par \par \uc2 -- Analysts say action comes as a warning but too soon to tell if crisis will come to a head\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    By William Sposato \par    Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 TOKYO (Dow Jones)--The dollar was lower against a resurgent euro and the safe-haven yen in early Asian trading Thursday after \f28 \uc2 \f2 Moody's\f28 \uc2 \f2  said it was putting U.S. Treasurys on review for a possible downgrade and Federal Reserve Chairman Ben Bernanke said the Fed may need to undertake a new round of easing.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The euro was also helped by an absence of bad news following a rash of negative headlines earlier in the week suggesting that the euro-zone debt problems were fast spreading. The EU is conducting stress tests on 91 European banks, with results due out Friday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 At 0050 GMT, the dollar was at Y78.73 from Y79.01 in late New York trade Wednesday, according to data from EBS. The euro posted strong gains to $1.4231 from $1.4158, and was at Y112.04 from Y111.82.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Moody's\f28 \uc2 \f2  said late Wednesday that it was putting its long-standing Aaa rating of Treasurys on review due to the ongoing political feud over raising the national debt limit.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Teppei Ino, senior analyst at \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of Tokyo-Mitsubishi\f28 \uc2 \f2  UFJ, said the move was a warning to politicians to come up with a deal.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "I don't think investors are going to sell U.S. Treasurys like crazy" due to the latest warning, he said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Attention is also on the Treasury Department's scheduled sale of $13 billion of 30-year bonds later in the global day, he said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The euro was also helped by comments from Bernanke leaving open the possibility of a third round of quantitative easing after recent poor U.S. economic data.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The strength of the yen has again raised the specter of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , following the coordinated move by the G-7 on March 18 when the yen rose sharply. Finance Minister Yoshihiko Noda said Thursday morning that the yen's recent moves were "far out of line with real fundamentals," ratcheting up the rhetoric.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "It's inevitable that Noda, as the point man on \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , has to try to talk the yen down like this, but I think it's unlikely that there'd be any \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  now as the Kan government doesn't have the political wherewithal for it," said Toshihiko Sakai, chief manager of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and financial products trading at Mitsubishi UFJ Trust and Banking.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Thai baht hit a two-month high against the greenback. Dealers said that the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of Thailand\f28 \uc2 \f2  was believed to have bought dollars at around THB30.01-30.05. The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was not available for comment. The dollar was later at BHT30.03 from BHT30.33 late Wednesday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Among other pairs, the dollar slid to its lowest level in nearly three years against the Korean won, at KRW1,054.00 from KRW1,060.60 on Wednesday. It also touched a record low of S$1.2158 from S$1.2233 late Wednesday against the Singapore dollar.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Among other \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , the U.K. pound was at $1.6162 after earlier hitting $1.6192, the highest since June 22, and compared with $1.6098 in late New York trade. The dollar was at CHF0.8117 from CHF0.8183.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The ICE Dollar Index was at 74.830 from 75.159 in New York.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Interbank \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Foreign Exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Rates At 20:50 EDT / 0050 GMT \par  \par  \par                            Latest       Previous   %Chg    Daily    Daily   %Chg \par Dollar Rates                               Close            High      Low  12/31 \par  \par USD/JPY Japan            78.72-74       78.98-09  -0.35    79.10    78.62  -2.95 \par EUR/USD Euro            1.4230-32      1.4158-64  +0.50   1.4282   1.4166  +6.27 \par GBP/USD U.K.            1.6160-64      1.6101-06  +0.36   1.6192   1.6106  +3.55 \par USD/CHF Switzerland     0.8115-20      0.8173-84  -0.75   0.8170   0.8088 -13.18 \par USD/CAD Canada          0.9575-80      0.9582-87  -0.07   0.9594   0.9564  -3.72 \par AUD/USD Australia       1.0764-68      1.0756-61  +0.07   1.0798   1.0744  +5.20 \par NZD/USD New Zealand     0.8475-80      0.8370-76  +1.25   0.8505   0.8350  +8.73 \par  \par Euro Rates \par  \par EUR/JPY Japan           112.02-06      111.81-89  +0.17   112.59   111.86  +3.13 \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By William Sposato, Dow Jones Newswires; 81-3-6269-2785; william.sposato@dowjones.com\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -Kosaku Narioka and Andrew Monahan contributed to this story [ 14-07-11 0134GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1034 1863 28038 4162   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110714e77e0003i\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
