\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  COLUMN-Investors should call Japan's bluff on yen\b0\par\par\uc2 592 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Juli 2011\par 07:34\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 -- Rick Lloyd is a Reuters \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  Analyst. The views expressed are his own --\par \par \uc2 By Rick Lloyd\par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE, July 13 (Reuters) - The last thing Japan needs is a stronger \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , just when its equity markets have started to rally and a recovery has quickened after March's devastating earthquake and tsunami.\par \par \uc2 In the past 24 hours Japanese officials have been trying to jawbone the yen lower after a series of stop-losses were triggered in thin trading that cut dollar/yen down to around 78.50, the lowest since March 17.\par \par \uc2 Outright \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  is unlikely at this point, and even if undertaken may not be so successful in keeping the yen at bay because of the immensity of the euro zone debt crisis that is driving flows back to the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Jawboning by officials will probably become clearer threats to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to cap the yen, but the market should call their bluff.\par \par \uc2 Unlike in March, the Japanese authorities would probably not get any help from other G7 rich nations to weaken the yen.\par \par \uc2 Europe has more than its fair share of problems right now and participating in euro buying against the yen or dollar at this point would not be high on their list of current priorities, especially since frankly they could use a weaker euro to boost competitiveness.\par \par \uc2 Tokyo Financial Exchange (TFX) data show the dollar/yen long position at a record level as of close of business yesterday, while the overall short yen position is some US$10.2 billion. TFX is only one retail \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  provider, suggesting the overall retail position could be some 10 times the TFX data and a significant headwind to the success of yen \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The selloff in dollar/yen and cross yen early this morning has no doubt stopped out a number of short yen positions, including some margin traders. But if history is a guide those positions will be reinstated quickly, if they have not already been put back on.\par \par \uc2 In addition, there are big reasons to think yen strength could be protracted.\par \par \uc2 For one, a combination of weak U.S. data (in particular last Friday's employment data ), the continued lack of agreement on the U.S. debt ceiling and worsening problems in peripheral Europe have driven market players into U.S. Treasuries, pushing yields down and cutting their yield advantage over Japanese government bonds.\par \par \uc2 Furthermore, a unilateral \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  could be even less effective than the effort last September. On that occasion they did one day of massive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , to the tune of JPY 2,125 billion, driving the dollar up by 3 big figures on the day. Within a week, though, the dollar's downtrend against the yen had resumed.\par \par \uc2 Any \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by MOF would most likely have even less impact, particularly as retail accounts have built up large short yen positions and would happily buy into any yen weakness.\par \par \uc2 Lastly, the ongoing woes in peripheral Europe will no doubt have an impact on both institutional and retail Japanese investors' appetite to own euro zone bonds. We can expect to see large scale repatriation as euro area bonds mature, especially if unresolved U.S. budget problems in the near term make shifting exposure to dollars unappealing.\par \par \uc2 Overall a strategy of selling into any rallies and certainly selling into \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in dollar/yen or cross yen should be favoured.\par \par \uc2 Reuters Messaging: rick.lloyd.reuters.com@reuters.net\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 /YEN (COLUMN)   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020110716e77d0003j\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
