\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Economic Stories Of The Day\b0\par\par\uc2 1,108 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Juli 2011\par 12:20\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par EURO-ZONE INDUSTRIAL OUTPUT ROSE SLIGHTLY IN MAY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Factories across the 17 countries that share the euro increased their output in May, but only slightly, raising fresh doubts about the strength of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  area's economic recovery. (published 1004 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par IEA:TO CAREFULLY ASSESS NEXT WEEK IF FURTHER STOCK RELEASE NEEDED \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The International Energy Agency said Wednesday it will assess next week whether it needs to release more oil from its emergency stocks, on top of a 60 million barrel release announced last month. (published 1036 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par ITALY'S BUDGET WILL BE TOUGHER, PASSED BY FRIDAY - FIN MIN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Italy's economy minister Wednesday said the country's four-year fiscal plan will be made more stringent. (published 1055 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par INVESTOR BUYING SUPPORTS ITALY, SPAIN BONDS, IRELAND WEAKER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Italian and Spanish bonds rose Wednesday as investors stepped back into the market following Tuesday's spectacular volatility. (published 0904 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par IEA: CHINA'S OIL DEMAND MAY RISE 5% IN 2012 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's oil demand will likely increase by 5% in 2012 as long as the country maintains its current rate of economic growth, the International Energy Association said Wednesday in a monthly oil market report. (published 0900 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par IEA DEFENDS OIL STOCK RELEASE AMID MORE BULLISH SUPPLY-DEMAND \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The International Energy Agency Wednesday issued a firm rebuttal to critics of its decision to release 60 million barrels of emergency oil stocks, saying the move is having the intended effect and pointing to a supply-demand balance that is growing steadily tighter. (published 0900 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA GDP GROWTH FASTER THAN EXPECTED, MAY TIGHTEN POLICY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China reported surprisingly robust economic growth for the second quarter, raising the prospect of further tightening to combat inflation. (published 0448 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par IRISH GOVERNMENT DERIDES MOODY'S DOWNGRADE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Irish finance ministry and the country's debt agency Wednesday joined in attacking on \f28 \uc2 \f2 Moody's\f28 \uc2 \f2  Investor Services, saying its downgrade of Ireland to junk status was unjustified. (published 0800 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par IRISH GOVERNMENT DERIDES MOODY'S DOWNGRADE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Irish finance ministry and the country's debt agency Wednesday joined in attacking on \f28 \uc2 \f2 Moody's\f28 \uc2 \f2  Investor Services, saying its downgrade of Ireland to junk status was unjustified. (published 0800 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par SPANISH INFLATION SLOWS IN JUNE BUT STAYS ABOVE AVERAGE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Spanish consumer-price inflation slowed sharply in June, due to lower rises in the price of tobacco, food and drinks, the country's National Statistics Institute, also known as INE, said Wednesday. (published 0800 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA OFFICIAL: RISK OF SHARP ECONOMIC SLOWDOWN IS 'SMALL' \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's overall economic performance is good despite falls in some indicators, and the risk of a sharp economic slowdown is "small," Sheng Laiyun, spokesman for the National Bureau of Statistics, said Wednesday. (published 0244 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par MEDVEDEV URGES BUSINESS TO PICK SIDES AHEAD OF POLLS: REPORT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 MOSCOW --Russian President Dmitry Medvedev urged top businessmen to decide who they want to see as the country's next president amid the uncertainty ahead of key polls, a report said Wednesday. (published 0658 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UK UNEMPLOYMENT BENEFIT CLAIMANTS SPIKE HIGHER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The number of people claiming jobless benefit in the U.K. posted its biggest increase for more than two years in June, but the wider unemployment rate dipped due to a rise in young people going into education, official data showed Wednesday. (published 0936 GMT)\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 JAPAN\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  FINANCE MINISTER CALLS YEN MOVES "ONE-SIDED," MUM ON \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's finance minister raised the volume on his warnings against the rising yen Wednesday, calling the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's recent moves "a little one-sided," while still maintaining a modest tone that suggests \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  isn't in the cards for now. (published 0450 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par JAPAN GOVERNMENT MAINTAINS VIEW OF ECONOMY IN JULY REPORT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's government said the nation's economy is still smarting four months after the March earthquake and tsunami, as electricity supply problems in the wake of the Fukushima Daiichi nuclear plant accident threaten improvement in production and exports. (published 0535 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par BOJ GOV SHIRAKAWA: BOJ ALONE CAN'T BEAT DEFLATION \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The governor of the Bank of Japan said Wednesday the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  alone can't fix the nation's entrenched deflation, countering views that it isn't doing enough to reverse a decade and a half of growth-hobbling price falls. (published 0456 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par BOJ POLICY BOARD MEMBERS RENEW OPPOSITION TO JGB UNDERWRITING \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Bank of Japan's two new policy board members Wednesday repeated their opposition to the idea of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  directly buying Japanese government bonds to help funding for post-quake reconstruction. (published 0107 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par PBOC OFFICIAL: INITIAL ESTIMATE OF CHINA 1H TOTAL NATIONAL FINANCING CNY7.7 TLN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 An initial estimate of China's total national financing came to CNY7.7 trillion in the first half of 2011, a senior official at the People's Bank of China said Wednesday. (published 0415 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par MOODY'S DOWNGRADES IRELAND TO JUNK, CITING BAILOUT NEED \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Moody's Investors Service downgraded Ireland's sovereign-debt ratings into junk territory, saying the country will likely need another round of official financing before it can rely on the private debt market. (published 2208 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par IMF SAYS ITALY NEEDS TO CUT PUBLIC DEBT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The International Monetary Fund said Tuesday that Italy needs to take decisive steps to cut budget deficits amid rising concerns that Europe's debt crisis could infect the continent's third-largest economy. (published 2342 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par    ======== DOW JONES NEWSWIRES ANALYSIS AND COMMENTARY ======== \par  \par EUROPEAN \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  TECHNICALS: EUR CORRECTS HIGHER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Intraday EUR/USD: There is scope for more corrective gains above 1.4054 towards the 1.4185 area. A break above 1.4054 is required to build on the recovery off Tuesday's 1.3837 low, but Monday's completion of a bear pennant keeps the downside threat prevalent, limiting the rally to the vicinity of the pennant breakout point at 1.4178. A push below 1.3935 would prompt a setback towards 1.3871, and only below the latter would re-expose the 1.3837 low. (published 0717 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par EUROPEAN INTEREST RATE TECHNICALS: CONSOLIDATES BENEATH HIGHS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Intraday BUND: A rounded bottom formation on the 60-minute chart is the foundation for a recovery towards 129.78. The 129.78 resistance area consists of intraday congestion highs and the 50% Fibonacci retracement level of the 130.91/128.59 decline. The structure of the decline off Tuesday's contract high at 130.91 suggests the 130.91 high is isolated, and only a move above 130.36 would bring it back into the picture. A push below 128.59 would attract further bear pressure towards 128.06 and 127.85. (published 0633 GMT) [ 13-07-11 1020GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1030 1804 4180   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110713e77d000t7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
