\par\par \b \uc2 Dow Jones Asia-Pacific Top Stories Sked For July 13\b0\par\par\uc2 1,977 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Juli 2011\par 09:08\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 Following are the top Asia-Pacific stories featured on Dow Jones Newswires as of 0700 GMT. Not all stories appear on all wires. Please direct any questions or comments to asianewseds@dowjones.com.\par \par \uc2 MACRO/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 /FIXED INCOME:\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par 3RD UPDATE: CHINA GDP GROWTH FASTER THAN EXPECTED, MAY TIGHTEN POLICY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China reported surprisingly robust economic growth for the second quarter, raising the prospect of further tightening to combat inflation. (published 0448 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 JAPAN\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  FINANCE MINISTER CALLS YEN MOVES "ONE-SIDED," MUM ON \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's finance minister raised the volume on his warnings against the rising yen Wednesday, calling the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's recent moves "a little one-sided," while still maintaining a modest tone that suggests \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  isn't in the cards for now. (published 0450 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par JAPAN GOVERNMENT MAINTAINS VIEW OF ECONOMY IN JULY REPORT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's government said the nation's economy is still smarting four months after the March earthquake and tsunami, as electricity supply problems in the wake of the Fukushima Daiichi nuclear plant accident threaten improvement in production and exports. (published 0535 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par BOJ GOV SHIRAKAWA: BOJ ALONE CAN'T BEAT DEFLATION \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The governor of the Bank of Japan said Wednesday the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  alone can't fix the nation's entrenched deflation, countering views that it isn't doing enough to reverse a decade and a half of growth-hobbling price falls. (published 0456 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par BOJ POLICY BOARD MEMBERS RENEW OPPOSITION TO JGB UNDERWRITING \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Bank of Japan's two new policy board members Wednesday repeated their opposition to the idea of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  directly buying Japanese government bonds to help funding for post-quake reconstruction. (published 0107 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: PBOC OFFICIAL: INITIAL ESTIMATE OF CHINA 1H TOTAL NATIONAL FINANCING CNY7.7 TLN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 An initial estimate of China's total national financing came to CNY7.7 trillion in the first half of 2011, a senior official at the People's Bank of China said Wednesday. (published 0415 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: CHINA PROPERTY INVESTMENT, SALES STAY STRONG IN JUNE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Property investment and sales in China remained robust last month, indicating that the government is unlikely to ease the various tightening measures aimed at slowing the rapid rise in house prices in the country. (published 0559 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par 2ND UPDATE: S KOREA JUNE JOBLESS RATE 3.3%; JOBS GROW MOST SINCE JULY 2010 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korea's unemployment rate held steady in June from the previous month as Asia's fourth-largest economy added the most number of jobs since July 2010, the government said Wednesday. (published 0142 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par AUSTRALIA'S JULY CONSUMER SENTIMENT INDEX -8.3% ON JUNE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 An index of consumer sentiment in Australia plummeted 8.3% in July from June, marking the lowest reading in the index in two years, as the ramifications of heightened European debt concerns and a controversial carbon tax soiled household views. (published 0046 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par NEW ZEALAND JUNE FOOD PRICE INDEX UP 1.4% VS MAY, UP 7.5% ON YEAR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 New Zealand's food price index rose 1.4% in June from May and was up 7.5% on the year, Statistics New Zealand said Wednesday. (published 2324 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par PHILIPPINE \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CENTRAL BANK\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  FLAGS POSSIBLE TIGHTENING AT NEXT MEET \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Philippine \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on Wednesday flagged a possible tightening at its policy meeting later this month amid concerns about strong capital flows. (published 0429 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par WORLD BANK: PHILIPPINES NEEDS TO IMPROVE INVESTMENT CLIMATE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Philippines will have to improve governance and open key sectors of the economy to attract more foreign investment, the country representative of the World Bank said Wednesday. (published 0346 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par PREVIEW: INDIA WHOLESALE PRICES LIKELY UP 9.70% IN JUNE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 India's inflation likely accelerated in June as persistent demand pressure and a hike in the prices of auto and cooking fuels stoke price pressures in the economy. (published 0607 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 EQUITIES:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par 2ND UPDATE: \f28 \uc2 \f2 MITSUI & CO\f28 \uc2 \f2  MAKES S$221 MLN RIVAL BID FOR PORTEK INTERNATIONAL \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Mitsui & Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Wednesday it is making a S$221 million offer for \f28 \uc2 \f2 Portek International Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., challenging \f28 \uc2 \f2 International Container Terminal Services Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2 .'s S$180.5 million standing offer for the Singapore-listed port operator. (published 0634 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA TELECOM: TALKS WITH APPLE ON IPHONE STILL ONGOING; NO TIMETABLE FOR LAUNCH \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China Telecom Corp. Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Wednesday it is in talks with \f28 \uc2 \f2 Apple Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2 . about offering the iPhone in China. (published 0254 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA TELECOM: SHANG BING RESIGNS AS PRESIDENT, EFFECTIVE WEDNESDAY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China Telecom Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Wednesday its president and chief operating officer, Shang Bing, has resigned, with immediate effect. (published 0452 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: CITIC SECURITIES 1H NET PROFIT UP 13% AT CNY2.97 BLN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Citic Securities (600030.SH) said Wednesday its net profit in the first half of this year rose 13% to CNY2.97 billion (US$459.0 million) from CNY2.63 billion a year earlier. (published 0540 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UNIASIA COSMETICS PLANS TO RAISE UP TO US$200 MLN IN HK IPO - SOURCE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Uniasia Cosmetics Holdings Ltd. plans to raise around US$150 million-US$200 million in an initial public offering ahead of listing on the Hong Kong stock exchange in September, a person familiar with the situation said Wednesday. (published 0501 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par NUFARM FY11 UNDERLYING NET OPERATING EARNINGS EXPECTED A$88M-94M \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Crop protection company \f28 \uc2 \f2 Nufarm Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . estimated Wednesday that underlying net operating earnings for this fiscal year will settle within a range of A$88 million to A$94 million, jumping from an actual A$58.6 million last fiscal year ended July 31, 2010, amid varying operating conditions. (published 2348 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par HYNIX, TOSHIBA AGREE TO JOINTLY DEVELOP NEXT GENERATION MEMORY TECHNOLOGY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Memory-chip maker \f28 \uc2 \f2 Hynix Semiconductor Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2 . and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Toshiba Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . jointly agreed to develop a next-generation memory technology and extended their cross licensing pact and product supply agreements, the companies said Wednesday. (published 0549 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par TEMASEK CHINA HEAD: NOT GOING TO SELL AGRICULTURAL BANK OF CHINA STAKE -REPORT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The China head of the Singapore's state-owned investment firm \f28 \uc2 \f2 Temasek Holdings Pte. Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said the firm is not going to sell its stake in \f28 \uc2 \f2 Agricultural Bank of China Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., Chinese news portal Sina.com reported Wednesday. (published 0638 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par INDIA INVITES BIDS FROM BANKERS FOR BHARAT HEAVY SHARE SALE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Indian government Wednesday invited bids from investment bankers to manage state-owned \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bharat Heavy Electricals Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 .'s public share sale. (published 0443 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 MITSUBISHI MOTORS\f28 \uc2 \f2 : AGREE WITH NISSAN TO PRODUCE PICKUP TRUCKS IN THAILAND \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Mitsubishi Motors Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . has agreed to produce pickup trucks for \f28 \uc2 \f2 Nissan Motor Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . at its plant in Thailand starting in fiscal 2012, the two companies said Wednesday. (published 0633 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par SK INNOVATION TO USE SALE PROCEEDS FOR NEW OIL BLOCKS, M&A DEALS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SK Innovation Co. Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., South Korea's largest oil refiner by capacity, said Wednesday it will use the proceeds from the sale of its Brazilian division worth $2.4 billion for the acquisition of new oil blocks and M&A deals with foreign companies. (published 0001 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par NTPC CHAIRMAN: PLAN TO BID FOR BANDANNA ENERGY STAKE BY JULY 29 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 NTPC Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . plans to make a final bid for a stake in Australian miner \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bandanna Energy Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . by July 29, the Indian power producer's chairman and managing director said Wednesday. (published 0633 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par INTERVIEW: UNITED TELELINKS PLANS TO SELL 15% STAKE FOR INR6 BILLION \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Unlisted United Telelinks Ltd.--the maker of Karbonn branded mobile phones--is planning to sell a 15% stake in the company to private equity firms for INR6 billion as the Indian handset maker seeks to expand its business in the world's fastest-growing telecommunications market. (published 0659 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par DR REDDY'S GETS US OK TO SELL GENERIC INJECTION TO PREVENT BLOOD CLOTS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Dr. Reddy's Laboratories\f28 \uc2 \f2  Ltd. said Wednesday it has received final approval from the U.S. Food and Drug Administration to sell a generic version of \f28 \uc2 \f2 GlaxoSmithKline PLC\f28 \uc2 \f2 's Arixtra injection, which prevents blood clots after surgery. (published 0457 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par BELLE CORP BOARD APPROVES DETAILS OF STOCK RIGHTS ISSUE PLAN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Belle Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Wednesday its board has approved details of its stock rights issue plan, which is expected to raise PHP4.525 billion for the company. (published 0152 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 POWER FINANCE CORP\f28 \uc2 \f2  CHAIRMAN: AIM TO RAISE INR300 BLN THIS FISCAL YEAR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Indian state-run lender \f28 \uc2 \f2 Power Finance Corp. Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . aims to raise a total of INR300 billion in the current financial year through March 2012, Chairman \f28 \uc2 \f2 Satnam Singh\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Wednesday. (published 0526 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 MOTHERSON SUMI SYSTEMS\f28 \uc2 \f2 : TO BUY 80% OF PEGUFORM GROUP FROM CROSS INDUSTRIES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Auto parts maker \f28 \uc2 \f2 Motherson Sumi Systems Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . Wednesday agreed to purchase an 80% stake in Germany's Peguform Group from \f28 \uc2 \f2 Cross Industries AG\f28 \uc2 \f2  for an undisclosed amount. (published 0550 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par AUSTRALIA REGULATOR INVESTIGATES INSIDER TRADING \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australia's securities regulator said Wednesday it investigated 17 matters of potential insider trading and six of market manipulation in the first half of this year. (published 0049 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par BUKIT ASAM CEO: 1H NET PROFIT LIKELY ABOVE IDR1.5 TLN VS IDR909 BLN 1H 2010 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 PT Tambang Batubara Bukit Asam\f28 \uc2 \f2 's first-half net profit likely rose to more than IDR1.5 trillion during from IDR909 billion a year earlier, boosted by higher coal sales volume and price, Chief Executive Sukrisno said Wednesday. (published 0418 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par BERJAYA CORP SIGNS INITIAL PACT WITH POSCO ENGINEERING & CONSTRUCTION \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Malaysia's \f28 \uc2 \f2 Berjaya Corp. Bhd\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Wednesday it has signed an initial pact with South Korea's \f28 \uc2 \f2 Posco Engineering & Construction Co. Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . for collaboration on projects relating to engineering, construction, and development. (published 0503 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: ASIAN SHARES MOSTLY HIGHER; CHINA DATA ALLAY SLOWDOWN FEARS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Asian stock markets were mostly higher Wednesday after stronger-than-expected data in China allayed concerns about a slowdown in growth in the world's second largest economy. (published 0357 GMT) [ 13-07-11 0708GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ENERGY/COMMODITIES:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: OIL DATA: JAPAN CRUDE STOCKS DOWN, DOMESTIC DEMAND UP \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's crude-oil inventories fell below 17 million kiloliters last week for the first time in four weeks as domestic demand for some refined products inched upward with the arrival of summer. (published 0431 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: OIL DATA: CHINA JUNE CRUDE-OIL OUTPUT 4.19 MLN B/D \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China produced 17.15 million metric tons of crude oil in June, or 4.19 million barrels a day, up 1.6% from a year earlier and 1.7% higher than May, data from the National Bureau of Statistics showed Wednesday. (published 0347 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: OIL DATA: CHINA JUNE REFINERY RUNS LOWEST IN 9 MONTHS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's refinery run rates in June fell to their lowest level in nine months, reflecting heavy maintenance at domestic refineries and weaker demand for crude due to high international prices and slower industrial activity. (published 0556 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: CHINA JUNE CRUDE STEEL OUTPUT HITS RECORD, RENEWS CONCERNS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's daily crude steel output in June rose to a record average of 2 million metric tons as steelmakers ran mills near full capacity, despite weaker demand in some key end-user segments, to maximize profits amid falling margins. (published 0419 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: CHINA JUNE COPPER, ALUMINUM OUTPUT HIT RECORD HIGHS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's copper production hit a new record high in June as smelters continued to ramp up production on the back of sufficient concentrate supply and higher copper prices. (published 0601 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: CHINA 2011 CORN OUTPUT LIKELY TO RISE 2.4% -CNGOIC \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China raised its output forecasts for key grain sectors Wednesday, increasing its outlook for corn production by 2.4% from last year to 181.5 million metric tons. (published 0339 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA STEEL: GLOBAL STEEL DEMAND LIKELY STAGNANT IN 3RD QUARTER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China Steel Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., Taiwan's biggest steelmaker by revenue, said Wednesday that global steel demand will likely be stagnant in the third quarter of the year as customers typically keep inventories at low levels during the period. (published 0637 GMT) [ 13-07-11 0708GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 62550   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110713e77d000hs\par }\page {\p