on and exports. (published 0535 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par BOJ GOV SHIRAKAWA: BOJ ALONE CAN'T BEAT DEFLATION \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The governor of the Bank of Japan said Wednesday the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  alone can't fix the nation's entrenched deflation, countering views that it isn't doing enough to reverse a decade and a half of growth-hobbling price falls. (published 0456 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par BOJ POLICY BOARD MEMBERS RENEW OPPOSITION TO JGB UNDERWRITING \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Bank of Japan's two new policy board members Wednesday repeated their opposition to the idea of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  directly buying Japanese government bonds to help funding for post-quake reconstruction. (published 0107 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UPDATE: PBOC OFFICIAL: INITIAL ESTIMATE OF CHINA 1H TOTAL NATIONAL FINANCING CNY7.7 TLN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 An initial estimate of China's total national financing came to CNY7.7 trillion in the first half of 2011, a senior official at the People's Bank of China said Wednesday. (published 0415 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UPDATE: CHINA PROPERTY INVESTMENT, SALES STAY STRONG IN JUNE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Property investment and sales in China remained robust last month, indicating that the government is unlikely to ease the various tightening measures aimed at slowing the rapid rise in house prices in the country. (published 0559 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par 2ND UPDATE: S KOREA JUNE JOBLESS RATE 3.3%; JOBS GROW MOST SINCE JULY 2010 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korea's unemployment rate held steady in June from the previous month as Asia's fourth-largest economy added the most number of jobs since July 2010, the government said Wednesday. (published 0142 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par AUSTRALIA'S JULY CONSUMER SENTIMENT INDEX -8.3% ON JUNE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 An index of consumer sentiment in Australia plummeted 8.3% in July from June, marking the lowest reading in the index in two years, as the ramifications of heightened European debt concerns and a controversial carbon tax soiled household views. (published 0046 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par 2ND UPDATE: MOODY'S DOWNGRADES IRELAND TO JUNK, CITING BAILOUT NEED \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Moody's Investors Service downgraded Ireland's sovereign-debt ratings into junk territory, saying the country will likely need another round of official financing before it can rely on the private debt market. (published 2208 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UPDATE: IMF SAYS ITALY NEEDS TO CUT PUBLIC DEBT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The International Monetary Fund said Tuesday that Italy needs to take decisive steps to cut budget deficits amid rising concerns that Europe's debt crisis could infect the continent's third-largest economy. (published 2342 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par NEW ZEALAND JUNE FOOD PRICE INDEX UP 1.4% VS MAY, UP 7.5% ON YEAR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 New Zealand's food price index rose 1.4% in June from May and was up 7.5% on the year, Statistics New Zealand said Wednesday. (published 2324 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par PHILIPPINE \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CENTRAL BANK\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  FLAGS POSSIBLE TIGHTENING AT NEXT MEET \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Philippine \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on Wednesday flagged a possible tightening at its policy meeting later this month amid concerns about strong capital flows. (published 0429 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par WORLD BANK: PHILIPPINES NEEDS TO IMPROVE INVESTMENT CLIMATE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Philippines will have to improve governance and open key sectors of the economy to attract more foreign investment, the country representative of the World Bank said Wednesday. (published 0346 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par    ======== DOW JONES NEWSWIRES ANALYSIS AND COMMENTARY ======== \par  \par  \par AUSTRALIAN DOLLAR'S METEORIC RISE RAISES ALARMS FOR INVESTORS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Some big investors are starting to worry about the Australian dollar, a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  that has soared 75% against its U.S. peer since the depths of the financial crisis. (published 2311 GMT) [ 13-07-11 0600GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1030 1804 4180   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110713e77d000b5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
