\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Japan \highlight\uc2  MOF Data Shows No  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  In  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  Market May 28-June 28\b0\par\par\uc2 185 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 Juni 2011\par 12:20\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2011, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 TOKYO -(Dow Jones)- \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  authorities didn't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market in the May 28-June 28 period, data released from the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  showed Thursday. The outcome was expected by market participants.\par \par \uc2 The latest data confirm that the ministry hasn't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market since March 18, when it sold Y692.5 billion as a part of international efforts to tame the yen's strength.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 , using the Bank of Japan as its agent, stepped into the market March 18 after the Group of Seven nations agreed on a rare concerted \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  campaign.\par \par \uc2 The greenback hit a record low of Y76.25 on March 17. As of 1001 GMT, the dollar was at Y80.41.\par \par \uc2 Thursday's data cover trades settled in June. Trades in the spot market are settled after two business days.\par \par \uc2 -By Kosaku Narioka, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-6269-2784; kosaku.narioka@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 June 30, 2011 06:20 ET (10:20 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020110630e76u002g5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
