\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Economic Stories Of The Day\b0\par\par\uc2 743 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Juni 2011\par 14:02\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par TOP STORIES \par  \par EUROGROUP TO SET GREEK BAILOUT PLAN BY EARLY JULY \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Euro-zone finance ministers say they have narrowed their differences over how to get Greece's private-sector creditors to contribute to the country's financing in coming years. The ministers aim to have a final plan in place "by early July."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par US STOCK FUTURES LOWER AS MARKETS TRACK EURO LOSSES \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.S. stock futures are pointing to a lower open for Wall Street, with markets expected to track losses in Europe after a weekend meeting of euro-area finance ministers fail to wipe out fears of a Greek default.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par OIL DOWN AS DOLLAR STRENGTHENS ON GREEK DEBT WORRIES \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Oil futures recover slightly from an earlier drop to a fresh four-month low as the euro weakened against the dollar as finance ministers met for a second day to hash out an agreement on the Greek sovereign debt crisis.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par EURO-ZONE CURRENT ACCOUNT DEFICIT WIDENS \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The euro zone's current account deficit widens to \u8364\'20\'AC5.1 billion in April as the balance of trade for goods swung into negative territory, European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  data shows.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par ALMOST 70% OF CHINA'S \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  RESERVES IN DOLLARS \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.S. dollar assets account for nearly 70% of China's massive \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves, a researcher at a prominent Chinese government think tank says in a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 -run publication.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par JAPAN RAISES ECONOMIC VIEW AS SUPPLY CHAINS RECOVER \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Japanese government raises its economic assessment for the first time in four months as quake-disrupted supply chains continue to recover, adding to a growing consensus that the country is bouncing back from the March 11 disaster.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par G7 WANT SOLID PLAN OF PRIVATE CREDITORS IN GREEK DEBT \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A discussion among the G7 included the Greek political situation, contagion risk and plans for the participation of private bond holders in a new bailout package, a senior euro-zone official says.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par SANTANDER DENIES TALKS WITH QATAR \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Spanish bank Banco Santander denies it is holding talks with Qatar, Reuters reports. Media reports earlier said Qatar's sovereign wealth fund was looking at a stake in Santander's U.K. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par PNC TO PAY $3.45B FOR RBC'S US UNIT \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 PNC Financial Services Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  confirms its acquisition of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Royal Bank of Canada\f28 \uc2 \f2 's U.S. retail banking unit for $3.45 billion. PNC beat out rival regional bank \f28 \uc2 \f2 BB&T\f28 \uc2 \f2  for the RBC \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par REPORT JAPAN PM AGREES CONDITIONS FOR DEPARTURE \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan Prime Minister Naoto Kan agreed to step down after securing parliamentary passage of the second extra budget and a bill authorizing the issuance of deficit-covering bonds, though the timing of his resignation remains unclear, the Asahi Shimbun reports.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par  \par  \par    ======== DOW JONES NEWSWIRES ANALYSIS AND COMMENTARY ======== \par  \par Money Talks \par GREECE WILL DEFAULT, BUT NOT YET \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The current rescue plans of the EU, IMF and ECB are merely mechanisms designed to postpone Greece's day of reckoning by loading the country up with yet more debt, writes Alen Mattich.\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Focus \par DOLLAR'S Y80 FLOOR MAY NOT HOLD NOW \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 For weeks, the U.S. and Japanese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  have traded in a narrow range against each other, trapped on one side by optimism over a U.S. recovery and limited on the other by fears of Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . But, Nicholas Hastings writes that these key factors could be changing.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Analysis \par JAPAN \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  POLICY SEEN STEADY IF NODA BECOMES PM \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  policy would likely stay unchanged if Finance Minister Yoshihiko Noda becomes the country's next prime minister, Takashi Nakamichi writes.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par The Wall Street Journal \par CHINA LEADERS LAUD "RED" CAMPAIGN \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 When Bo Xilai, a rising star in the Communist Party, began sending mass text messages with Maoist slogans, few people elsewhere in China took it seriously. Three years on, Bo's "red" campaign is sweeping the nation, writes Jeremy Page.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par   ============ MARKETS ACTION ============ \par  \par US STOCK FUTURES LOWER; MARKETS SEEN TRACKING EURO LOSSES \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Stock futures down as markets expected to track euro losses.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par US TREASURYS WELL BID \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 US Treasurys show strength but trading volume is low.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par GREEK IMPASSE HITS EURO, YET AGAIN \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Greek debt crisis continues to weigh on the euro.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par OIL DOWN AS DOLLAR STRENGTHENS ON GREEK DEBT WORRIES \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Oil futures recover slightly from an earlier drop as the euro weakened against the dollar.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par SPOT GOLD DOWN, BUT SUPPORTED BY GREECE WOES \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Spot gold is slightly lower in Europe, weighed by a weaker euro. [ 20-06-11 1202GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1030 1804 4180   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110620e76k000v3\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
