\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2  FOCUS: Dollar's Y80 Floor May Not Hold Now\b0\par\par\uc2 574 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Juni 2011\par 13:01\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 --Soft US data suggest Fed will keep policy easy\par \par \uc2 --Stronger Japanese data point to earlier recovery\par \par \uc2 --Cost of stronger yen may not be so high\par \par \uc2 By Nicholas Hastings\par \par \uc2 A DOW JONES NEWSWIRES COLUMN\par \par \uc2 LONDON (Dow Jones)--A serious break for the dollar under Y80 is more likely now.\par \par \uc2 For weeks, the U.S. and Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  have traded in a narrow range against each other, trapped on one side by optimism over a U.S. recovery and limited on the other by fears of Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 However, both of these key factors could be changing.\par \par \uc2 In the case of the U.S. recovery, recent economic data show that the upturn is proving much more gradual than expected and that the chances of the Fed starting to tighten policy have receded rapidly.\par \par \uc2 If anything, the Fed is expected to confirm at its latest policy meeting on Wednesday that, although QE2 has formally ended this month, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will maintain the current level of liquidity by reinvesting its maturing bond purchases.\par \par \uc2 For the moment, the Fed is denying any suggestion that it is entertaining another dose of quantitative easing, or QE3, but recent data showing that the economy is stalling in the middle of 2011 very much as it did in the middle of 2010, means that talk of further easing will increase.\par \par \uc2 This is coinciding with more evidence that Japan is recovering from the ill-effects of its devastating earthquake and tsunami in the middle of March much more rapidly than anticipated.\par \par \uc2 The Japanese government acknowledged this by raising its review of the economy for the first time in four months.\par \par \uc2 Even initially disappointing trade numbers, showing a further widening in the county's trade deficit, could be read as helpful as imports rose 2.4% on the month, indicating that domestic demand continues to improve.\par \par \uc2 However, exports were also up a little on the month, suggesting both that global demand might be stabilizing and that the yen's recent strength against the dollar may not be so damaging after all.\par \par \uc2 If the improved Japanese data further reduce speculation that the Bank of Japan will have to ease its monetary policy at the same time that the Fed is seen postponing any of its plans to tighten policy, then yield differentials are likely to continue working in the yen's favor.\par \par \uc2 However, further yen gains against the dollar are still likely to be constrained by fears of Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  if the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  starts to fall under Y80.\par \par \uc2 This has been a key level ever since a sharp rally in the yen immediately after the earthquake prompted market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and its leading western counterpart.\par \par \uc2 Now, though, the Bank of Japan could prove a little more tolerant of yen strength if the Japanese economy is proving more resilient than expected and Japanese exports aren't suffering as much as many had feared.\par \par \uc2 Bloomberg TNI FRX POV\par \par \uc2 Reuters USD/DJ\par \par \uc2 Thomson P/1066 or P/1074\par \par \uc2 (Nicholas Hastings is a Senior Correspondent in London for Dow Jones Newswires who has written about \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  for more than 20 years. He previously covered a variety of markets, including equities, fixed income, commodities and energy. He can be contacted on +44-20-7842-9493 or by email: nick.hastings@dowjones.com) [ 20-06-11 1101GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1066   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110620e76k000sl\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
