\par\par \b \uc2 Dow Jones Asia-Pacific Top Stories Sked For June 20\b0\par\par\uc2 2,216 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Juni 2011\par 09:06\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 Following are the top Asia-Pacific stories featured on Dow Jones Newswires as of 0700 GMT. Not all stories appear on all wires. Please direct any questions or comments to asianewseds@dowjones.com.\par \par \uc2 MACRO/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 /FIXED INCOME:\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: JAPAN POSTS DEEP TRADE DEFICIT IN MAY ON QUAKE IMPACT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan posted a Y853.7 billion trade deficit in May, the government said Monday, the biggest shortfall in nearly two and a half years as the impact of the March 11 earthquake and tsunami continues to inhibit a recovery in the nation's economy. (published 0153 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par JAPAN GOVT EDANO: LOW TRADE NUMBERS EXPECTED DUE TO DISASTER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's top government spokesman said Monday that the country's deep trade deficit in May was expected due to the impact of the March 11 earthquake and tsunami. (published 0235 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par INTERVIEW: FITCH: SEE SERIOUS INFLATION PRESSURES IN CHINA \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China faces serious longer-term inflationary challenges, and it is important that it uses interest rates to a greater extent to control pressures, an analyst at Fitch Ratings said Monday. (published 0512 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: CHINA RAIN THREATENS VEGETABLE OUTPUT, RAISES PRICES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Heavy rain has reduced vegetable output by about 20% from levels a year earlier in key Chinese provinces and pushed grain and vegetable prices higher, posing a threat to government efforts to raise the quantity of domestic produce amid inflationary pressures. (published 0452 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par DOLLAR ASSETS ACCOUNT FOR ALMOST 70% OF CHINA'S \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  RESERVES - THINK TANK RESEARCHER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.S. dollar assets account for nearly 70% of China's massive \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves, a researcher at a Chinese government think-tank wrote in a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central-bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  run publication Thursday. (published 0630 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par INTERVIEW: FITCH: S KOREA BANKS' SHORT-TERM EXTERNAL DEBT BACK ON RISE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Fitch Ratings is closely watching the short-term external debt of South Korean banks as it remains a key factor in determining the nation's sovereign credit ratings, Fitch's Asia Pacific Head of Sovereign Ratings Andrew Colquhoun said Monday. (published 0247 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par RBI'S GOKARN: TO END RATE HIKES ONCE CORE INFLATION STABILIZES AT 4%-4.5% - REPORT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 India's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will end its rate-tightening cycle once non-food manufacturing, or core, inflation stabilizes around 4%-4.5%, a report cited Deputy Governor Subir Gokarn as saying. (published 0310 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA MAY RAISE INTEREST RATES 2-3 MORE TIMES THIS YEAR - REPORT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China may raise interest rates another two or three times this year to contain rising inflation, the state-run Shanghai Securities News reported Monday, citing a senior government think-tank official. (published 0050 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par JAPAN PM KAN AGREES ON SOME CONDITIONS FOR STEPPING DOWN-REPORT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japanese Prime Minister Naoto Kan has agreed to step down after securing parliamentary passage of the second extra budget and a bill authorizing issuance of deficit-covering bonds for the current fiscal year, though the timing of his resignation remains unclear, the Asahi Shimbun reported Monday, without citing sources. (published 0652 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par WSJ: LOW-KEY POLITICIAN POISED TO SUCCEED NAOTO KAN AS JAPAN'S PREMIER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Yoshihiko Noda is hardly a household name in Japan, but that may be about to change as the lawmaker is increasingly seen as a party front-runner to succeed the prime minister. (published 0655 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: JAPAN AUTO INDUSTRY WARNS ON STRONG YEN'S IMPACT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The chairman of the Japan Automobile Manufacturers Association said Monday the yen's current level is "not acceptable," warning that any loss of competitiveness overseas due to the stubbornly strong \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  could result in job losses in the industry. (published 0654 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: THAILAND SWINGS BACK TO TRADE SURPLUS; BOT TIPPED TO HIKE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Thailand's trade balance swung back to a surplus of $277.5 million in May, with ongoing export growth likely to encourage the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of Thailand\f28 \uc2 \f2  to continue its monetary policy tightening efforts to curb accelerating inflation. (published 0446 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par NEW ZEALAND PM ESTIMATES EARTHQUAKE COSTS AT 8-9% OF GDP \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 New Zealand Prime Minister John Key Monday said his government estimates recent earthquakes in the country will cost between 8% and 9% of national output. (published 0256 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par NEW ZEALAND'S FONTERRA YUAN BOND CLOSES 6 TIMES OVERSUBSCRIBED \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 New Zealand's Fonterra Co-Operative Group Ltd. said Monday its US$42 million 3-year yuan bond was six times oversubscribed. (published 0616 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: BEIJING ENTERPRISES WATER PLANS YUAN-DENOMINATED BOND \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Beijing Enterprises Water Group Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Monday it plans to offer fixed rate, yuan-denominated bonds to fund capital expenditure and for general working capital. (published 0318 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par INDONESIA DELAYS GLOBAL SUKUK OFFER TO OCTOBER FROM JULY - OFFICIAL \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Indonesian government has delayed the planned offering of its first global sukuk to September or October from July or August as it is still seeking parliamentary approval for the offering, a senior official at the finance ministry told reporters Monday. (published 0337 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par JAPAN \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  POLICY LIKELY STEADY IF NODA BECOMES PM \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japanese Finance Minister Yoshihiko Noda may have helped execute two dramatic \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 -market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  during his tenure, but that doesn't mean that should he become the next prime minister, his government would be more aggressively \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventionist\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . (published 0055 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par PASSION LIES BENEATH BLAND EXTERIOR OF \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 JAPAN\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  PM CANDIDATE NODA \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Yoshihiko Noda is hardly a household name in Japan, but that may be about to change dramatically. (published 0135 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par PREVIEW: AUSTRALIAN \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CENTRAL BANK\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  MINUTES MAY HAVE A NEW TWIST \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australia's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will signal Tuesday that interest rates are set to rise in coming months but, to be safe, leave some room for disappointment. (published 0624 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par PREVIEW: HK INFLATION LIKELY HIT 34-MONTH HIGH IN MAY ON FOOD, RENT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Hong Kong's inflation likely rose to a 34-month high in May because of higher rents and food prices, economists said. (published 0345 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par PREVIEW: MALAYSIA INFLATION LIKELY ROSE 3.3% ON YEAR IN MAY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Malaysia's consumer price inflation likely continued to edge up in May, with the government's decision to reduce subsidies putting additional pressure on already high food and transport costs, economists said. (published 0300 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 EQUITIES:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: SUN ART RETAIL SEEKS US$1 BLN FROM HK IPO; HOSA BEGINS BOOKBUILDING - SOURCES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Chinese hypermarket operator Sun Art Retail Group Ltd. has started pre-marketing its around US$1 billion initial public offering in Hong Kong ahead of a listing on the Hong Kong stock exchange on July 15, a person familiar with the situation said Monday, the latest big IPO in the city despite a recent market slowdown and weak debuts from recent share sales. (published 0418 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: KOREA AEROSPACE PRICES $523.8 MLN IPO NEAR TOP OF INDICATIVE RANGE - SOURCE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Aircraft manufacturer \f28 \uc2 \f2 Korea Aerospace Industries Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 .'s initial public offering is set to raise KRW567.52 billion after it was priced Monday near the top of an indicative range, a person familiar with the situation said, marking the largest local IPO since \f28 \uc2 \f2 Samsung Life Insurance Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . raised KRW4.89 trillion in April 2010. (published 0649 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par HOSA INTERNATIONAL STARTS HK IPO ROADSHOW; TO RAISE UP TO US$242M - TERM SHEET \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Hosa International Ltd., a Chinese sportswear maker, is raising up to US$242 million from a Hong Kong initial public offering, according to a term sheet seen by Dow Jones Newswires on Monday. (published 0225 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: CALTEX FORECASTS 1H PROFIT DROP; SHARES PLUNGE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Caltex Australia Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . on Monday disappointed investors by forecasting an up to 39% fall in first half profit, dragged down by high oil prices, a strong Australian dollar and refinery outages. (published 0252 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par PANASONIC EXPECTS FY GROUP NET PROFIT Y30.00B \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Panasonic Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Monday it expects its net profit to fall 59% in the current fiscal year through March 2012, as the Japanese electronics giant continues to cope with the impact of the March 11 disaster on the country's supply chain. (published 0641 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par SAMSUNG: TO LAUNCH JAPAN COMMERCIAL LTE SERVICE IN 2012 WITH \f28 \uc2 \f2 KDDI\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Samsung Electronics Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., an advanced network solutions company, said Monday it will launch a commercial long term evolution, or LTE, service in Japan jointly with \f28 \uc2 \f2 KDDI Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . in 2012. (published 0239 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ASX LTD\f28 \uc2 \f2  APPROVES CHI-X APPLICATION TO CLEAR, SETTLE TRADES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australian stock exchange operator ASX Ltd. on Monday approved an application by \f28 \uc2 \f2 Nomura Holdings Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2 .'s Chi-X to clear and settle the rival's trades in Australia. (published 0156 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par MINERAL DEPOSITS IN TRADING HALT; POTENTIAL JV, CAPITAL RAISING \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Mineral sands miner \f28 \uc2 \f2 Mineral Deposits Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . entered a trading halt on the Australian Securities Exchange early Monday, pending an announcement on a potential joint venture and capital raising. (published 2342 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par STX TO BUILD $1 BLN SHIPYARD FOR RUSSIA'S STATE-RUN SHIPBUILDER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 STX Group said Monday it had signed an initial agreement with \f28 \uc2 \f2 United Shipbuilding Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . to build a $1 billion shipyard in St. Petersburg for the Russian state-run shipbuilder. (published 0047 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par NISSAN, \f28 \uc2 \f2 MITSUBISHI MOTORS\f28 \uc2 \f2  JV: HOPE TO COOPERATE ON ELECTRIC CARS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A joint venture to develop mini vehicles set up by \f28 \uc2 \f2 Nissan Motor Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Mitsubishi Motors Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . seeks to develop electric vehicles in the future, the venture's chief operating officer said Monday. (published 0655 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par METRO HOLDINGS: PROPOSES TO SELL 50% STAKE IN HUAMAO PROPERTY FOR CNY688.6M \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Singapore-listed Metro Holdings Ltd. plans to sell its 50% stake in Huamao Property Co., the owner of the Metro City Beijing commercial property, for CNY688.6 million, the group said in a statement issued Sunday. (published 2321 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: VIRGIN AUSTRALIA CANCELS FLIGHTS AS VOLCANIC ASH CLOUD RETURNS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Virgin Australia Ltd. said Monday it will suspend flights to Adelaide and Mildura on Tuesday as dust from a Chilean volcano returns. (published 0649 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par SHUI ON CONSTRUCTION TO SELL 49% OF PROPERTY SITE FOR CNY440 MLN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 20-06-11 0706GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Property developer \f28 \uc2 \f2 Shui On Construction & Materials Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said it has agreed to sell 49% of a site in China's Chengdu city for CNY440 million . (published 0050 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par ST ENGINEERING: AEROSPACE ARM TO FORM JV WITH \f28 \uc2 \f2 MARUBENI CORP\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Singapore Technologies Engineering Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . Monday said it aerospace unit has formed a 50-50 aircraft engine leasing joint venture with Japan's \f28 \uc2 \f2 Marubeni Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . . (published 2339 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: ASIAN SHARES MIXED; UTILITIES SUPPORT TOKYO; SENSEX DROPS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Asian stock markets were mixed Monday, as initial support from hopes for a resolution to Greece's debt crisis faded, with gains for utility stocks underpinning the Tokyo market, while Indian shares dropped sharply. (published 0518 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ENERGY/COMMODITIES:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par BHP BILLITON'S ESCONDIDA MINE IN CHILE HALTED BY BAD WEATHER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 BHP Billiton Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . is waiting for an update on conditions at Chile's Escondida, the world's largest copper mine, after it temporarily suspended \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  due to bad weather, a spokeswoman said Monday. (published 0046 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: OIL DATA: JAPAN MAY LNG IMPORTS UP; NUCLEAR CAPACITY IDLED \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's liquefied natural gas imports rose 26% in May, as utilities boosted thermal power generation to partially offset nuclear power capacity they have reduced amid rising concerns over atomic energy safety. (published 0406 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par REFINERY WATCH: TAIWAN JULY OIL PRODUCTS EXPORTS DOWN SLIGHTLY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Taiwanese refiners plan to process similar amounts of crude-oil in July than in June, but their exports of petroleum products will fall slightly. (published 0610 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par SPECULATIVE NET LONGS IN SUGAR UP ALMOST 50% ON MONTH SINCE MAY 14 -ANZ \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Speculative net long positions in sugar futures in the month ended June 14 stood at 155,000 contracts, up almost 50% in the previous four weeks, ANZ Commodities Research said in a report Monday, citing data from the U.S. Commodity Futures Trading Commission. (published 0255 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA COPPER IMPORTS TO FALL AS TIGHTER CREDIT WEIGHS ON DEMAND \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Tighter credit conditions in China will reduce the country's copper imports going forward as slowing demand can be met mainly with existing stocks and domestic output, industry participants said. (published 0609 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: JAPAN-INDONESIA CONSORTIUM TO BUILD COAL-FIRED PLANT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A consortium comprising \f28 \uc2 \f2 Electric Power Development Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., or J-Power, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Itochu Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . and \f28 \uc2 \f2 PT Adaro Energy\f28 \uc2 \f2  has obtained preemptive rights to negotiate building a coal-fired power plant in Indonesia via a tender, J-Power and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Itochu\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Monday. (published 0623 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: AUSTRALIA'S GREENS, INDEPENDENTS WANT BAN ON ANIMAL EXPORTS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Two separate pieces of legislation will be introduced into Australia's House of Representatives on Monday, both aiming to end the export of live animals for slaughter. (published 0217 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par AUSTRALIAN FARM MIN TO HOLD TALKS IN JAKARTA ON CATTLE TRADE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australia's Agriculture Minister Joe Ludwig will hold talks with his Indonesian counterpart and officials in Jakarta on Monday about the future of live cattle exports after Australia suspended the trade earlier in June. (published 0030 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par BHP BILLITON COMMITTED TO ITS YEELIRRIE URANIUM PROJECT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 BHP Billiton Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . Monday downplayed speculation on the future of a uranium project being developed in west Australia, although construction work on a mine may be delayed. (published 0646 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: CHINA RAIN THREATENS VEGETABLE OUTPUT, RAISES PRICES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Heavy rain has reduced vegetable output by about 20% from levels a year earlier in key Chinese provinces and pushed grain and vegetable prices higher, posing a threat to government efforts to raise the quantity of domestic produce amid inflationary pressures. (published 0452 GMT) [ 20-06-11 0706GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 62550   \par \par \uc2 D