\par\par \b \uc2 DJ MARKET TALK: STI Flat Midday; 3100 Support Tipped As Key\b0\par\par\uc2 2,099 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Juni 2011\par 06:46\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2011, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in Singapore. 65 64154 140; MarketTalk@dowjones.com \par  \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 0446 GMT [Dow Jones] Singapore's STI is flat at 3101.82 midday, off its intraday high at 3114. After a resilient start, the index has pulled back as markets in Hong Kong and Shanghai trade lower and amid weak sentiment as Wall Street maintained its losing streak Wednesday. The benchmark index is just above support at 3100, a level UOB KayHian says "will be closely watched as any decline beyond (here) will signify more downside risks." \uc2 OCBC Bank\uc2  says the next support below the 3100 mark is around 3070, "and we caution that volatility may remain prevalent as investors continue to revise their perspectives on the U.S. economic prospect going forward." Market volume picks up slightly to 616 million shares, helped by Artivision's (5NK.SG) 77 million, after it resumed trade on announcing a S$2.5 million private placement; the shares are up 7.7% at S$0.210. This afternoon \uc2 Perennial China Retail Trust\uc2  (N9LU.SG) will grab some attention when it makes its debut after a S$776.2 million initial public offering, priced at S$0.70/unit. (matthew.allen@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0436 GMT [Dow Jones] The KLCI is up 0.1% at 1553.37 midday, with oil and gas companies lending support. Traders say the oil and gas stocks are up after state oil and gas company \uc2 Petronas\uc2  says it will award its next risk service contract within the next 60 days, and also raised its capital expenditure plan to MYR300 billion over the next five years. A local dealer says, "The volumes are really low, and the broader sentiment remains cautious." He tips a 1550-1560 range for the day. Market breadth is negative with 304 decliners vs 263 gainers. \uc2 Petronas Dagangan\uc2  (5681.KU) is up 0.8% at MYR16.12, \uc2 Petronas Chemicals\uc2  (5183.KU) is up 0.7% at MYR7.01 and \uc2 Petronas Gas\uc2  (6033.KU) is up 0.3% at MYR11.62. Among decliners \uc2 UMW Holdings\uc2  (4588.KU) is down 0.8% at MYR7.19, \uc2 MMC Corp\uc2 . (2194.KU) is down 0.7% at MYR2.76 and \uc2 Tenaga Nasional\uc2  (5347.KU) is down 0.3% at MYR6.87. (ankur.relia@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0433 GMT [Dow Jones] Malaysia's weaker-than-expected April industrial production numbers may give Bank Negara cause to "consider the possibility of a pause" in monetary tightening at its next meeting in July, says Affin Investment economist Alan Tan. April industrial output shrank 2.2% on year, compared with +2.7% forecast in a Dow Jones poll; March's IPI was +2.9% on year. He says the numbers are a "surprise" as growth was expected due to 2010's lower base. "The impact of the Japan earthquake and weaker demand for E&E (electrical and electronic products) was obviously greater than expected," Tan says. This will translate to weaker 2Q GDP growth vs 1Q's +4.6%, he says. But Tan adds, he's keeping his forecast for a 25bp rate hike to 3.25% in the benchmark OPR in July for now, as inflation remains a key concern for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Malaysia's May CPI data is due on June 22. (kwan-por.lee@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0429 GMT [Dow Jones] The Sensex is +0.2% at 18,427.19, led by gains in \uc2 Reliance Industries\uc2  (500325.BY). A local analyst tips the market to move sideways in the morning session and investors will take their cues from European markets in the afternoon session. Likely triggers in the coming sessions are factory output data for April due Friday, and May inflation data and the outcome of the RBI's rate-setting meeting next week, he adds. \uc2 Reliance Industries\uc2  is +0.8% at INR954.85 on bargain-buying. Among losers, Maruti Suzuki (532500.BY) is off 1.1% at INR1,212.20 as a workers strike at a plant enters the fifth day. \uc2 Reliance Communications (532712.BY) \uc2 is down 1.3% at INR93.00 on profit-taking after Wednesday's 2.5% gain. Among non-Sensex laggards, \uc2 Mahanagar Telephone Nigam\uc2  (500108.BY) is down 2.1% at INR44.00 and HCL Infosystems (500179.BY) is 6.7% lower at INR97.55 after a federal body probing allegations of irregularities in Commonwealth Games contracts files a case against the two. ICICIdirect.com tips the Sensex to find support at 18,340 and resistances at 18,540.(sudeep.jain@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0429 GMT [Dow Jones] Malaysia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is still expected to raise its key policy rate at its next monetary policy meeting in July, despite the on-year contraction in April industrial output, says Irvin Seah, an economist at DBS Bank in Singapore; "this (industrial output) is certainly lower-than-expected and is to a large extent due to the electronic supply chain disruptions arising from the earthquake in Japan." But Seah adds, a weak 2Q GDP has more or less been priced-in by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and they are taking a longer term view on the balance between growth and inflation. He expects \uc2 Bank Negara Malaysia\uc2  to raise its overnight policy rate by another 25 bps in July, after hiking by 25 bps in May to 3.00%. Malaysia's industrial output shrank 2.2% in April from a year earlier, led lower by the manufacturing and mining sectors. Twelve economists polled by Dow Jones Newswires had given a median forecast of 2.7% growth.(ankur.relia@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0428 GMT [Dow Jones] The USD/KRW is building on earlier modest gains as the Kospi's fall steepens, with the index off 0.6%, while offshore players remain largely biased toward bidding up the USD, possibly on global economic recovery concerns, traders say; the pair is up at 1,084.00 from 1,083.20 earlier and 1,080.10 late Wednesday in Seoul. A second attempt at testing the 1,085 resistance is eyed for the rest of the session after the pair's failure to breach that level near the market open; a breakthrough of that level could lead to a brief spike in the pair to as high as 1,088 or 1,089, traders add. Still, players "are intent on buying the dollar near the low-1,080s region and then selling around the upper-1,080s," in general, says a local bank trader. The pair is likely to touched its low for the day at 1,082, he notes. (min-jeong.lee@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0419 GMT [Dow Jones] Jim Rogers, an all time dollar bear and noted commodities and \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  investor, is currently long the U.S. dollars because he believes it's time to rally when 95% of the people, including him are bearish. Indeed some traders say there may have been too much of a one-sided short-sell on the USD. The dollar index rose 0.4% on Wednesday after failing to break below near the 5-week low of 73.500 Tuesday. "USD position has been too skewed to the short side and when there are blips in risk sentiment and uncertainty revolving around Greece restructuring plans, the stretched dollar short position tends to get squeezed," says a trader in Taipei. The daily chart is showing some early signs of a possible swing higher with slow stochastic starting to rise at oversold levels and the negative Moving Average Convergence/Divergence, or MACD, histogram bars contracting. If the weekly close fail to close below Tuesday's low at 73.500, the dollar index could possibly be due for a rebound above 74.000 and possibly, toward 74.750, the 23.6% Fibonacci retracement of the decline from Nov. 30 high at 81.440 to May 4 low at 72.700 in weeks to come. (christopher.wong@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0416 GMT [Dow Jones] Japan's MOF sells Y2.19 trillion of 0.4% five-year bonds with a lowest price of 99.92, yielding 0.416%, slightly higher than traders' expectations of 99.91. "The auction went well, given that players chased for higher prices," says a Tokyo-based fund manager. "As the duration (of the easy monetary policy in Japan) is expected to be long and there appear to be concerns about a slowdown in the global economic recovery, players were eager to park their surplus cash in the medium-term sector," which is sensitive to changes in monetary policy. The bid-to-cover ratio was at 3.21 from 3.25 at the previous auction in May, while the tail shortened to 0.01 from 0.02 last month. (megumi.fujikawa@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0411 GMT [Dow Jones] The HSI falls 1.0% to 22,425.13 at midday as investors remain risk averse amid ongoing concerns about the U.S. economic outlook and the possibility of further tightening in China, says Alvin Cheung, associate director at Prudential Brokerage. The index falls below its 250-day moving average, or the so-called the 'bull-bear' threshold of 22,597 with its next support tipped at its year-to-date low of 22,123. "The recent trading pattern suggests that bearish sentiment is expected to linger in the near-term." HK developers are lower but faring better ahead of the much-awaited government land auction later in the day. Cheung Kong (0001.HK) is down 0.4% at HK$115.40, \uc2 Sino Land\uc2  (0083.HK) is down 0.3% at HK$12.94 and \uc2 Sun Hung Kai Properties\uc2  (0016.HK) is down 0.3% at HK$115.70. Trading volume is heavier than recent average at HK$40.78 billion. (susanna.tai@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0409 GMT [Dow Jones] Vietnam's worst may have passed, despite economic data remaining dire, Daiwa says in a report. The house notes May CPI inflation rose 19.8% on-year, while the trade deficit widened 20% on-year to US$6.6 billion, but the VND is stable and subsidy cuts are reining in the fiscal deficit. Daiwa expects rising inflation to prompt further rate hikes and projects the refinancing rate will rise another 200 bps by end-3Q11, before inflation begins to moderate in 4Q. It adds, tighter monetary policy and reduced government spending should slow 2011 real GDP growth; 1Q11 GDP rose 5.4% on-year vs 2010 GDP +6.8% on-year. Daiwa cuts its FY11 real GDP growth forecast to 5.8% on-year from 6.3% previously. "We view this as good news, because an economic slowdown is necessary to overcome the symptoms of overheating (inflation and trade deficit). If, as we expect, Vietnam can get its long-delayed privatization program off the ground, the clouds over the Vietnam economy would truly part." (leslie.shaffer@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 9 Jun 2011 00:46 EDT DJ  MARKET TALK: STI Flat Midday; 3100 Support Tipped -2-\par \par \uc2 0407 GMT [Dow Jones] Daiwa Securities Capital Markets says going forward, it believes Japanese shares will enter a rally once U.S. economic sentiment starts to pick up as it did in 1995. "We expect US weekly initial jobless claims to decline after rising in July as experience shows that claim numbers often increase in the first month of the quarter. All in all, we see a good entry opportunity around end-June for Japanese shares," the house said in a client note. The house points out that coordinated rate cuts and \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the U.S. and \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  preceded the U.S. economic recovery in 1995. It adds, however, that the yen appears set to gain in value again this time, but expects the Bank of Japan to take strong enough measures to keep the yen from rising above its record high (USD/JPY 76.25). (bradford.frischkorn@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0402 GMT [Dow Jones] The USD/INR is down as selling is led by one-off capital flows, while local stocks are in the green, says a senior dealer with a state-run bank. The pair is at 44.64, compared with 44.71 late Wednesday. "We anticipate inflows to be around $600 million, which should not push the pair sharply down," he says. Oil importers may come up to bid at lower levels, supporting the pair, he adds. He tips the pair in a 44.60-44.80 range for the session. (nupur.acharya@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 June 09, 2011 00:46 ET (04:46 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020110609e769000vl\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
