\par\par \b \uc2 WORLD  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 : Dollar Sinks To Fresh 1-Mo Low Vs Yen On Weak Stocks, US Econ\b0\par\par\uc2 By Tatsuo Ito   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 725 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Juni 2011\par 07:41\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 TOKYO (Dow Jones)--The dollar sank to a fresh one-month low against the yen in Asia Wednesday, with concerns about the U.S. economy and the lack of resilience in global stock markets prompting traders to sell the dollar and the euro for the yen to reduce risk.\par \par \uc2 The dollar fell as low as Y79.75 in Tokyo morning trade, the lowest since May 5. U.S. funds apparently gave up their long positions as the dollar's upside test ended in failure, triggering stop-loss sales, traders said.\par \par \uc2 At 0510 GMT, the dollar was at Y80.04 from Y80.10 in late New York Tuesday, according to EBS via CQG.\par \par \uc2 "A yen-buying trend, which we haven't seen for a while, is emerging," said Yoshio Yoshida, a trader at Mizuho Trust and Blanking Corp. "The failure of the recovery in the global stock market, partly due to the slowing U.S. economy, has induced yen-buying in crosses," Yoshida said. "If stock markets lose their ground, the yen should come under further upward pressure," he added.\par \par \uc2 Even though the dollar broke through the psychologically key Y80 mark and there may be further room to advance, traders and analysts here dismissed any imminent risk of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's finance ministry. The MOF last stepped into the market March 18 after the dollar fell to all-time low of Y76.25 the previous day.\par \par \uc2 "The yen remains weaker compared with that period. So it's hard to find good reasons to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  before the dollar falls to around Y76," Mizuho's Yoshida said.\par \par \uc2 Yuji Saito, \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market director at Credit Agricole in Tokyo, said that unless stock markets plunge, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is unlikely before the dollar falls to Y77.\par \par \uc2 A Nikkei fall below the 9000 may be a key factor in any \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , said Masafumi Yamamoto, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Barclays Bank in Tokyo.\par \par \uc2 At 0436 GMT, the Nikkei Stock Average was down 0.23% at 9421.48.\par \par \uc2 The European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will meet Thursday and President Jean-Claude Trichet is expected to signal that the ECB could raise rates in the coming months, as early as next month.\par \par \uc2 The chance is "very high" that the ECB will raise rates in July, as Greek's near-term debt problems could be settled at a meeting of eurozone finance ministers later this month, Saito said.\par \par \uc2 Mizuho's Yoshida said that since the market has factored in a rate hike in July, the euro may not be able to rally amid concerns about the global stock market, even if Trichet hints at a rate hike.\par \par \uc2 During Asian trade, the euro ran into profit-taking against the dollar. It was at $1.4670 from $1.4690 late New York trade Tuesday, and Y117.48 from Y117.65. The U.K. pound was at $1.6420 from $1.6449.\par \par \uc2 The ICE Dollar Index, which tracks the U.S. dollar against a basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , was at 73.631 against 73.533.\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Interbank \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Foreign Exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Rates At 00:50 EDT / 0450 GMT \par  \par                          Latest     Previous   %Chg   Daily   Daily    %Chg \par                                     2150 GMT          High    Low      12/31 \par USD/JPY Yen              79.94-96   80.03-07   -0.11  80.26   79.72    -1.57 \par EUR/USD Euro             1.4661-64  1.4689-92  -0.19  1.4693  1.4641   +9.66 \par GBP/USD Sterling         1.6421-23  1.6447-50  -0.16  1.6446  1.6404   +5.33 \par USD/CHF Swiss Franc      0.8372-78  0.8359-69  +0.16  0.8381  0.8357  -21.76 \par USD/CAD Canadian Dlr     0.9771-76  0.9744-50  +0.28  0.9791  0.9735   -2.58 \par AUD/USD Australian Dlr   1.0666-69  1.0717-22  -0.48  1.0723  1.0637   +8.99 \par NZD/USD New Zealand Dlr  0.8177-81  0.8204-06  -0.33  0.8213  0.8141   +5.01 \par  \par Euro Rate \par  \par EUR/JPY Yen              117.20-24  117.57-61  -0.31  117.85  116.88   +7.93 \par  \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Tatsuo Ito, Dow Jones Newswires; +813-6269-2780; tatsuo.ito@dowjones.com\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -Kosaku Narioka contributed to this article [ 08-06-11 0541GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1034 1863 28038 4162   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110608e768000as\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
