\par\par \b \uc2 *DJ  \highlight22\uc2 Japan \highlight\uc2  MOF Tamaki: March G-7  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Shows Yen Stability Important To Europe\b0\par\par\uc2 227 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Mai 2011\par 09:38\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2011, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 16 May 2011 04:10 EDT DJ  \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  MOF Tamaki: March G-7 \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  Shows Yen Stability Important To Europe\par \par \uc2 TOKYO (Dow Jones)--Japanese Vice Finance Minister For International Affairs Rintaro Tamaki said Monday the recent Group of Seven joint action to curb the yen's strength suggests the European authorities consider a stable yen "extremely important."\par \par \uc2 The joint \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 -market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Group of Seven leading industrialized nations on March 18 to curb the yen's strength "is a good example showing that the yen's stability is extremely important," not only for Japan but also for the 17-nation euro bloc, Tamaki said in a speech to a seminar.\par \par \uc2 The European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  decided "very quickly" to participate in the concerted action, even though as a rule, it must get approval from all of the euro-zone nations before conducting such market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Tamaki said.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's most powerful \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  bureaucrat, Tamaki played a key role in bringing the G-7 to an agreement in March to act together in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to counter a rising yen, according to Japanese government officials.\par \par \uc2 -By Takashi Nakamichi, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-6269-2781; takashi.nakamichi@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 May 16, 2011 04:10 ET (08:10 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020110516e75g001el\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
