\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Economic Stories Of The Day\b0\par\par\uc2 1,348 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Mai 2011\par 10:57\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 JAPAN\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  WATCHING YEN, BUT NO \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  THREATS--YET \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's finance minister said Friday he will carefully watch the rising yen, but stopped short of threatening \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 -market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in a sign that it may take sharper gains in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to spur Japanese action.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par EU TRADE COMMISSIONER DE GUCHT CALLS FOR 'REASONABLE' YUAN APPRECIATION \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's yuan should continue to appreciate at a "reasonable" pace, but that appreciation is a mixed bag for European economies, European Union Trade Commissioner Karel De Gucht said Friday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par ECB'S BONELLO: DIDN'T SEE NEED TO RAISE RATES IN MAY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Analysis of the latest inflation data shows that a further increase in interest rates wasn't warranted in May, European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  governing council member Michael Bonello said Friday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA SHARES END DOWN LED BY COAL, METAL STOCKS ON LOWER COMMODITY PRICES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's shares ended slightly lower Friday, led by coal and metal stocks, following sharply lower commodity prices overnight. (published 0838 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par JAPAN MONETARY BASE HITS RECORD HIGH IN APRIL ON POST-QUAKE FUND PROVISION \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's monetary base hit a record high in April, as the Bank of Japan pumped liquidity into the banking system after the March 11 earthquake raised concerns about the ability of banks to meet a surge in demand for funds from companies and households.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par ECB ORPHANIDES: MUST KEEP CLOSE EYE ON INFLATION EXPECTATIONS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  must keep a close eye on people's inflation expectations because they can be hard to predict, ECB Governing Council member Athanasios Orphanides said Friday. (published 0911 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par DATA SNAP: UK PRODUCER PRICES RISE FASTER THAN EXPECTED IN APR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.K. factory-gate prices rose faster than expected in April, pushed higher by a record increase in clothes prices. (published 0941 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par RUBLE FALLS SHARPLY VS DOLLAR ON OIL PLUNGE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The ruble dropped sharply Friday morning, as concerns of slowing global growth caused commodity prices to plummet, hitting a holiday-thinned Russian market. (published 0919 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par US, CHINA AGREE ON 'DIRECTION OF REFORM' FOR YUAN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The United States and China agree on the "direction of reform" for the yuan exchange rate, but with a different focus, Chinese Vice Finance Minster Zhu Guangyao said Friday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par ECB NOWOTNY: ECB'S STANCE ON INFLATION NOT DOVISH \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's stance on inflation shouldn't be seen as dovish, Ewald Nowotny, the ECB governing council member for Austria, said Friday. (published 0929 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par DATA SNAP: FRENCH BUDGET GAP WIDENS ON YEAR TO EUR33.6B END MAR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 France's budget deficit reached EUR33.6 billion at the end of March, wider than the same time last year due to exceptional items including cash advances to Greece, the budget ministry said Friday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par TURKISH LIRA UP AS OIL PRICE FALLS EASE PRESSURE ON DEFICIT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Sharp falls in the price of oil saw the Turkish lira strengthen early Friday as investors bet the commodity slide would ease pressure on Turkey's gaping current account deficit. (published 0931 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par AUSTRALIA'S RBA SIGNALS INTENTION TO HIKE RATES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australia's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Friday signaled its intention to raise interest rates in coming months to confront the scourge of rising inflation, putting aside short-term softness in parts of the economy harmed by a high Australian dollar.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par AUSTRALIAN SENATE BANK INQUIRY URGES ACTION ON MORTGAGE EXIT FEES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A number of recently proposed changes to Australia's banking rules are necessary, but any changes should be limited in number as competition and increased transparency are the best ways to generate improvements, the findings of an Australian Senate inquiry showed Friday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par DATA SNAP: SPAIN INDUSTRIAL PRODUCTION DOWN IN MARCH \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Spain's industrial output fell in March, a sign that the country's export-based recovery may be faltering. (published 0902 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par DATA SNAP: NORWAY MAR MANUFACTURING +0.9% ON MONTH,+3.0% ON YR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Norway's factory output rose in March in monthly and annual terms, data showed Friday. (published 0916 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par KOREA INVESTMENT CORP APPLIED FOR QFII STATUS IN CHINA IN OCTOBER - SOURCE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Korea Investment Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., South Korea's sovereign wealth fund, applied for a qualified foreign institutional investor license in China in October, a person familiar with the matter said Friday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par S KOREA GOVERNMENT TO SELL KRW2 TLN TREASURY BILLS IN MAY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The South Korean government will sell a total of KRW2 trillion in treasury bills via competitive bids in May, the Ministry of Strategy and Finance said Friday. (published 0856 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par S KOREA GOVT: TO RUN ECONOMIC POLICIES TO SUSTAIN RECOVERY BASED ON PRICE STABILITY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The South Korean government will run its micro- and macroeconomic policies to help sustain economic recovery based on price stability, the Ministry of Strategy and Finance reiterated Friday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par MALAYSIA MARCH EXPORTS UP 7.8% ON YEAR; BEAT FORECASTS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Malaysia's exports in March rose faster than analysts expected, indicating the trade-dependent country's economy likely grew strongly in the first quarter, which could push the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to raise interest rates again to contain rising inflation.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par MALAYSIA \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CENTRAL BANK\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  GOV: INTEREST RATES REMAIN SUPPORTIVE OF GROWTH \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Interest rates in Malaysia remain supportive of growth, the country's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  governor said Friday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par PHILIPPINES: INFLATION EXPECTED TO FALL WITHIN GOVERNMENT'S 3%-5% TARGET IN 2011, 2012 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Inflation in the Philippines is likely to fall within the government's 3% to 5% target range in 2011 and 2012, but the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will closely monitor emerging price pressures, according to a presentation Friday by the country's authorities at the Asian Development Bank's annual meeting.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par THAI PM: WILL SUBMIT PROPOSAL TO DISSOLVE PARLIAMENT LATER FRIDAY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Prime Minister Abhisit Vejjajiva said he will submit a decree on Friday afternoon to Thailand's king seeking royal endorsement for dissolving parliament, paving the way for a general election to be held by early July.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par BEIJING ENTERPRISES PRICES TWO-TRANCHE DOLLAR BOND - SOURCE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Beijing Enterprises Holdings Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . has priced a two-tranche dollar-denominated bond, raising $1 billion in the global offering, a person familiar with the offering said Friday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par FOSUN INTERNATIONAL TO ISSUE $300 MLN BOND DUE 2016 AT 7.5% A YEAR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Fosun International Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Friday it will issue $300 million of five-year bonds at 7.5% a year.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par PHILIPPINES PURISIMA: SAMURAI BOND STILL AN OPTION THIS YEAR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Philippine Finance Secretary Cesar V. Purisima said Friday that the country is still mulling a samurai bond, despite Japan's tragic earthquake, while a global peso offering could also be an option.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     ======= DOW JONES NEWSWIRES ANALYSIS AND COMMENTARY ======= \par  \par WORLD \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 : DOLLAR STEADY FOLLOWING GAINS IN WAKE OF COMMODITIES SELLOFF \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The dollar stabilized against other key \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in Asian trade Friday following sharp gains Thursday as a mass selloff in commodities pushed the greenback higher.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par HEARD ON THE STREET: A RATINGS JOLT FOR JAKARTA? \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Jakarta Composite Index gained more than 170% in 2009 and 2010. For the first few weeks of 2011 it slipped back on fears about inflation and potential monetary tightening before recovering, setting new records along the way. Jakarta's average multiple of 2011 earnings is about 15; richer than Thailand's 13 times and the multiple of 14 times in the Philippines.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA ENERGY WATCH: STATE GIANTS BUILDING UP TECHNICAL PROWESS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China is opening up another front in its campaign to play a greater role in the global energy industry, by honing technical skills to enable it to bid against Western companies for large-scale oil and gas infrastructure projects.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par PREVIEW: TAIWAN APRIL EXPORTS LIKELY REMAINED STRONG \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Taiwan's exports in April likely continued to grow robustly from a year earlier, helped by strong demand for the island's electronics products amid a strong global economic recovery and orders being shifted from Japan following March's earthquake.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par PREVIEW: INDIAN CONSUMER GOODS MAKERS' JAN-MARCH SALES LIKELY ROBUST \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 India's top two consumer goods makers by sales--\f28 \uc2 \f2 Hindustan Unilever Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . (500696.BY) and \f28 \uc2 \f2 ITC Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . (500875.BY)--are likely to report robust sales growth for the January-March quarter, but high raw materials costs could weigh on their operating margins. [ 06-05-11 0857GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1030 1804 4180   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110506e756000uw\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
