\par\par \b \uc2 Dow Jones Asia-Pacific Top Stories Sked For May 6\b0\par\par\uc2 2,226 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Mai 2011\par 09:03\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 Following are the top Asia-Pacific stories featured on Dow Jones Newswires as of 0700 GMT. Not all stories appear on all wires. Please direct any questions or comments to asianewseds@dowjones.com.\par \par \uc2 MACRO/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 /FIXED INCOME:\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 JAPAN\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  WATCHING YEN, BUT NO \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  THREATS--YET \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's finance minister said Friday he will carefully watch the rising yen, but stopped short of threatening \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 -market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in a sign that it may take sharper gains in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to spur Japanese action. (published 0550 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: AUSTRALIA'S RBA SIGNALS INTENTION TO HIKE RATES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australia's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Friday signaled its intention to raise interest rates in coming months to confront the scourge of rising inflation, putting aside short-term softness in parts of the economy harmed by a high Australian dollar. (published 0400 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: AUSTRALIAN SENATE BANK INQUIRY URGES ACTION ON MORTGAGE EXIT FEES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A number of recently proposed changes to Australia's banking rules are necessary, but any changes should be limited in number as competition and increased transparency are the best ways to generate improvements, the findings of an Australian Senate inquiry showed Friday. (published 0517 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par JAPAN MONETARY BASE HITS RECORD HIGH IN APRIL ON POST-QUAKE FUND PROVISION \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's monetary base hit a record high in April, as the Bank of Japan pumped liquidity into the banking system after the March 11 earthquake raised concerns about the ability of banks to meet a surge in demand for funds from companies and households. (published 0138 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par INTERVIEW: INDIA PRIME MINISTER'S ADVISER CUTS GROWTH ESTIMATE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The top economic adviser to the Indian prime minister has cut his estimate on the country's growth by half a percentage point, citing high inflation, and warned that ballooning subsidies will be a risk to the government's budget deficit target. (published 0643 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: US, CHINA AGREE ON 'DIRECTION OF REFORM' FOR YUAN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The United States and China agree on the "direction of reform" for the yuan exchange rate, but with a different focus, Chinese Vice Finance Minster Zhu Guangyao said Friday. (published 0417 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par EU TRADE COMMISSIONER DE GUCHT CALLS FOR 'REASONABLE' YUAN APPRECIATION \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's yuan should continue to appreciate at a "reasonable" pace, but that appreciation is a mixed bag for European economies, European Union Trade Commissioner Karel De Gucht said Friday. (published 0629 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: KOREA INVESTMENT CORP APPLIED FOR QFII STATUS IN CHINA IN OCTOBER - SOURCE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Korea Investment Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., South Korea's sovereign wealth fund, applied for a qualified foreign institutional investor license in China in October, a person familiar with the matter said Friday. (published 0503 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par S KOREA GOVT: TO RUN ECONOMIC POLICIES TO SUSTAIN RECOVERY BASED ON PRICE STABILITY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The South Korean government will run its micro- and macroeconomic policies to help sustain economic recovery based on price stability, the Ministry of Strategy and Finance reiterated Friday. (published 0039 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: MALAYSIA MARCH EXPORTS UP 7.8% ON YEAR; BEAT FORECASTS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Malaysia's exports in March rose faster than analysts expected, indicating the trade-dependent country's economy likely grew strongly in the first quarter, which could push the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to raise interest rates again to contain rising inflation. (published 0527 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par PHILIPPINES: INFLATION EXPECTED TO FALL WITHIN GOVERNMENT'S 3%-5% TARGET IN 2011, 2012 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Inflation in the Philippines is likely to fall within the government's 3% to 5% target range in 2011 and 2012, but the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will closely monitor emerging price pressures, according to a presentation Friday by the country's authorities at the Asian Development Bank's annual meeting. (published 0250 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par BANK INDONESIA GOVERNOR: CORE INFLATION NOT EXERTING PRESSURE FOR RATE HIKE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Bank Indonesia Governor Darmin Nasution said Friday that the current level of core inflation isn't yet exerting pressure for a rate hike, though he was quick to warn that inflationary pressures persist. (published 0616 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: THAI PM: WILL SUBMIT PROPOSAL TO DISSOLVE PARLIAMENT LATER FRIDAY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Prime Minister Abhisit Vejjajiva said he will submit a decree on Friday afternoon to Thailand's king seeking royal endorsement for dissolving parliament, paving the way for a general election to be held by early July. (published 0427 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par BEIJING ENTERPRISES PRICES TWO-TRANCHE DOLLAR BOND - SOURCE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Beijing Enterprises Holdings Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . has priced a two-tranche dollar-denominated bond, raising $1 billion in the global offering, a person familiar with the offering said Friday. (published 0106 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par FOSUN INTERNATIONAL TO ISSUE $300 MLN BOND DUE 2016 AT 7.5% A YEAR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Fosun International Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Friday it will issue $300 million of five-year bonds at 7.5% a year. (published 0103 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par PREVIEW: TAIWAN APRIL EXPORTS LIKELY REMAINED STRONG \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Taiwan's exports in April likely continued to grow robustly from a year earlier, helped by strong demand for the island's electronics products amid a strong global economic recovery and orders being shifted from Japan following March's earthquake. (published 0311 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par PREVIEW: INDIAN CONSUMER GOODS MAKERS' JAN-MARCH SALES LIKELY ROBUST \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 TAKING THE PULSE: India's top two consumer goods makers by sales--\f28 \uc2 \f2 Hindustan Unilever Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . and \f28 \uc2 \f2 ITC Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . --are likely to report robust sales growth for the January-March quarter, but high raw materials costs could weigh on their operating margins. (published 0653 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 EQUITIES:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: EVERBRIGHT BANK PLANS TO SEEK LISTING APPROVAL IN EARLY JUNE FOR HK IPO - SOURCE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China Everbright Bank Co., which could raise over US$6 billion in a Hong Kong initial public offering, plans to seek a listing approval from the Hong Kong stock exchange in early June, a person familiar with the situation said Friday. (published 0444 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par YOUKU.COM, INVESTORS PLAN UP TO $600 MLN SHARE OFFERING \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Chinese online video company \f28 \uc2 \f2 Youku.com Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said it and some of its investors plan to sell up to $600 million worth of American Depositary Shares in the company, with the majority of the offering composed of primary shares issued by \f28 \uc2 \f2 Youku\f28 \uc2 \f2 . (published 0308 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par 2ND UPDATE: KDB FINANCIAL MAY BID FOR SEOUL'S WOORI FINANCE STAKE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 State-owned \f28 \uc2 \f2 KDB Financial Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Friday it is considering a bid for the South Korean government's $6.2 billion majority stake in Woori Finance Holdings Co., a tie-up that would be a tacit acknowledgement of Seoul's inability to divest from its significant ownership of the local financial sector. (published 0623 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par MACQUARIE, CARLYLE RAISE OFFER FOR REDFLEX ON A$ STRENGTH \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Redflex Holdings Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., which makes red-light and speed infringement cameras, said Friday a consortium of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Carlyle Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Macquarie Group Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . have increased their takeover offer to around A$303.5 million to account for a stronger Australian dollar. (published 2309 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 MALAYAN BANKING\f28 \uc2 \f2  UNIT TO MAKE TENDER OFFER FOR THAI KIM ENG SECURITIES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A wholly owned unit of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Malayan Banking Bhd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . will make a tender offer for \f28 \uc2 \f2 Kim Eng Securities\f28 \uc2 \f2  's shares at THB16 each, the Thai brokerage said in a statement to the Stock Exchange of Thailand Friday. (published 0338 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par WSJ 2nd UPDATE: SONY CEO CALLS CYBER ATTACK 'FRUSTRATING TIME' FOR CUSTOMERS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Sony Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . Chief Executive \f28 \uc2 \f2 Howard Stringer\f28 \uc2 \f2  apologized for a massive data breach of the company's online game networks-- the first public remarks by the top executive as \f28 \uc2 \f2 Sony\f28 \uc2 \f2  works to reassure its customers following the theft of personal data from more than 100 million online accounts. (published 0228 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par FAST RETAILING: DOMESTIC UNIQLO SAME STORE SALES UP 4.6% IN APRIL ON YR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's \f28 \uc2 \f2 Fast Retailing\f28 \uc2 \f2  Co. said Friday that domestic same-store sales in April at its Uniqlo casual clothing chain grew 4.6% on year, rising for the first time in three months. (published 0616 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par SINGTEL OPTUS: REGIONAL AUSTRALIANS TO GAIN EARLY NBN ACCESS UNDER A$200M DEAL \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SingTel\f28 \uc2 \f2 's Australian subsidiary Optus said Friday it will provide satellite Internet services to regional and remote Australians in a 200 million Australian dollar deal with the company rolling out the nation's high-speed Internet network. (published 0616 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UNITED OVERSEAS BANK 1ST-QUARTER NET S$612 MLN VS S$700 MLN; EXPECTED S$620 MLN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 United Overseas Bank Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . Friday reported a larger-than-expected 12.6% fall in its first-quarter net profit due to weakness in its net-interest and non-interest income streams. (published 0454 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 MANILA ELECTRIC\f28 \uc2 \f2  1ST-QUARTER NET PROFIT UP 6.1% AT PHP2.13 BLN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Manila Electric Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., the country's largest power distributor by sales, said Friday its first-quarter net profit rose 6.1% to PHP2.13 billion from PHP2.01 billion a year earlier, because the effect of an increase in distribution charges outweighed flat electricity sales and a decline in revenue. (published 0442 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: MUTHOOT MAKES POSITIVE DEBUT AMID WEAK DEMAND FOR FINANCIAL STOCKS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Muthoot Finance Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . made a positive debut Friday on India's stock exchanges with the attractive growth prospects of the niche gold-backed financing firm offsetting weak demand for financial shares amid rising interest rates. (published 0639 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: \f28 \uc2 \f2 JINDAL STEEL\f28 \uc2 \f2 : NO DECISION YET ON POWER UNIT'S IPO TIMING \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Jindal Steel & Power Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . hasn't yet decided on a date for a planned initial public offering of its power unit to raise up to INR72 billion, its finance director said Friday. (published 0627 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 KINGFISHER AIRLINES\f28 \uc2 \f2  CEO: YET TO DECIDE ON GDR ISSUE TIMING \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 06-05-11 0703GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Kingfisher Airlines Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., India's second-biggest airline by market share, said Friday it is yet to decide on the timing for its planned issue of global depositary receipts. (published 0636 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par GLENMARK SETTLES NYCOMED LAWSUIT; TO SELL ANTI-INFLAMMATORY LOTION UNDER LICENSE PACT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Glenmark Pharmaceuticals Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . Friday said it has reached an agreement to resolve a patent lawsuit related to its new drug application to sell the generic version of Nycomed's anti-inflammatory Cutivate lotion in the U.S. (published 0344 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par SOHO CHINA: TO BUY PROPERTY IN SHANGHAI FOR CNY3.2 BLN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Soho China Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Friday it has agreed to buy a property in Shanghai for CNY3.2 billion, marking the company's seventh acquisition in the city. (published 0432 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par DBS: IN PACT WITH SUMITOMO TRUST AND BANKING TO DEEPEN COOPERATION IN ASIA \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 DBS Group Holdings Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . and \f28 \uc2 \f2 The Sumitomo Trust and Banking Co., Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . have signed an agreement to deepen cooperation in Asia. (published 0520 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par ASTRA CEO: LOWER 2Q CAR SALES WON'T GREATLY AFFECT FY11 EARNINGS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 PT Astra International\f28 \uc2 \f2  expects second-quarter car sales to drop by 15% from 109,069 units in the same period a year earlier due to a short supply from Japan after a massive earthquake in March. (published 0654 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: ASIAN SHARES MOSTLY DOWN; COMMODITY PLAYS BATTERED \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Asian stock markets were mostly lower Friday, with commodity-related stocks battered after oil and metals prices dropped sharply Thursday following weaker-than-expected U.S. jobless claims data. (published 0500 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ENERGY/COMMODITIES:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par TEPCO FINDS VALVE GLITCH AT KASHIWAZAKI KARIWA NUCLEAR PLANT, NO RADIATION LEAK \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Tokyo Electric Power Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Friday it found a glitch with one of the valves that helps pump cooling water into the No. 1 reactor of the Kashiwazaki Kariwa nuclear power plant in Niigata prefecture, northern Japan. (published 0437 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par TOHOKU ELECTRIC: TO RESTART MOTHBALLED POWER UNIT IN LATE MAY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Tohoku Electric Power Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Friday it will restart the mothballed 350-megawatt Minato No. 1 unit at its Higashi Niigata thermal power station in Niigata prefecture in northwestern Japan in late May, a little earlier than the previously expected timeframe of early June. (published 0456 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA COMMODITIES IN SELLOFF ON US CUES, DOMESTIC OVERSUPPLY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's metals and agriculture complex was in full retreat Friday, tracking sharp overnight losses in U.S. commodity and equity markets as a stronger dollar compounded oversupply and macroeconomic concerns at home. (published 0230 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: TOCOM RUBBER FALLS 8.7% ON HEIGHTENED RISK AVERSION \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Natural rubber futures on the Tokyo Commodity Exchange fell as much as 8.7% Friday amid risk aversion, after weaker-than-expected U.S. jobless claims data Thursday dragged down U.S. stocks and sparked heavy selloffs in oil and metals. (published 0311 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par 2ND UPDATE: BG GROUP, \f28 \uc2 \f2 CHUBU ELECTRIC\f28 \uc2 \f2  SEAL LNG SUPPLY PACT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 BG Group PLC\f28 \uc2 \f2  and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Chubu Electric Power Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Friday that they have signed a binding deal under which BG will sell Chubu up to 122 cargoes, or about 8.54 million metric tons, of liquefied natural gas over 21 years, starting in 2014. (published 0653 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: CITIC RESOURCES, BATHURST RESOURCES INK INITIAL COAL OFFTAKE DEAL \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Citic Resources Holdings Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Friday it has signed a preliminary agreement with \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bathurst Resources Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . for offtake from Bathurst's Buller coking coal project in New Zealand. (published 0543 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par NOVELIS TO INVEST $400 MLN TO INCREASE CAPACITY IN SOUTH KOREA \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Novelis Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., a unit of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Hindalco Industries Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., said late Thursday it will invest $400 million to expand its South Korean aluminum rolling and recycling \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to meet growing demand in Asia. (published 0354 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: INDIA MONSOON RAINS LIKELY TO ARRIVE ON TIME - OFFICIALS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 India's crucial monsoon rains are progressing well, according to early signs, and are likely to reach the country's Andaman and Nicobar Islands by their usual date of May 20, two weather officials said Friday. (published 0534 GMT) [ 06-05-11 0703GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 62550   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110506e756000m3\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
