\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Economic Stories Of The Day\b0\par\par\uc2 861 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Mai 2011\par 08:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UPDATE: \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 JAPAN\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  WATCHING YEN, BUT NO \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  THREATS--YET \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's finance minister said Friday he will carefully watch the rising yen, but stopped short of threatening \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 -market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in a sign that it may take sharper gains in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to spur Japanese action. (published 0550 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UPDATE: AUSTRALIA'S RBA SIGNALS INTENTION TO HIKE RATES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australia's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Friday signaled its intention to raise interest rates in coming months to confront the scourge of rising inflation, putting aside short-term softness in parts of the economy harmed by a high Australian dollar. (published 0400 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UPDATE: AUSTRALIAN SENATE BANK INQUIRY URGES ACTION ON MORTGAGE EXIT FEES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A number of recently proposed changes to Australia's banking rules are necessary, but any changes should be limited in number as competition and increased transparency are the best ways to generate improvements, the findings of an Australian Senate inquiry showed Friday. (published 0517 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par JAPAN MONETARY BASE HITS RECORD HIGH IN APRIL ON POST-QUAKE FUND PROVISION \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's monetary base hit a record high in April, as the Bank of Japan pumped liquidity into the banking system after the March 11 earthquake raised concerns about the ability of banks to meet a surge in demand for funds from companies and households. (published 0138 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UPDATE: US, CHINA AGREE ON 'DIRECTION OF REFORM' FOR YUAN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The United States and China agree on the "direction of reform" for the yuan exchange rate, but with a different focus, Chinese Vice Finance Minster Zhu Guangyao said Friday. (published 0417 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UPDATE: KOREA INVESTMENT CORP APPLIED FOR QFII STATUS IN CHINA IN OCTOBER - SOURCE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Korea Investment Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., South Korea's sovereign wealth fund, applied for a qualified foreign institutional investor license in China in October, a person familiar with the matter said Friday. (published 0503 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par S KOREA GOVT: TO RUN ECONOMIC POLICIES TO SUSTAIN RECOVERY BASED ON PRICE STABILITY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The South Korean government will run its micro- and macroeconomic policies to help sustain economic recovery based on price stability, the Ministry of Strategy and Finance reiterated Friday. (published 0039 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UPDATE: MALAYSIA MARCH EXPORTS UP 7.8% ON YEAR; BEAT FORECASTS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Malaysia's exports in March rose faster than analysts expected, indicating the trade-dependent country's economy likely grew strongly in the first quarter, which could push the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to raise interest rates again to contain rising inflation. (published 0527 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par MALAYSIA \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CENTRAL BANK\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  GOV: INTEREST RATES REMAIN SUPPORTIVE OF GROWTH \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Interest rates in Malaysia remain supportive of growth, the country's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  governor said Friday. (published 0246 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par PHILIPPINES: INFLATION EXPECTED TO FALL WITHIN GOVERNMENT'S 3%-5% TARGET IN 2011, 2012 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Inflation in the Philippines is likely to fall within the government's 3% to 5% target range in 2011 and 2012, but the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will closely monitor emerging price pressures, according to a presentation Friday by the country's authorities at the Asian Development Bank's annual meeting. (published 0250 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UPDATE: THAI PM: WILL SUBMIT PROPOSAL TO DISSOLVE PARLIAMENT LATER FRIDAY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Prime Minister Abhisit Vejjajiva said he will submit a decree on Friday afternoon to Thailand's king seeking royal endorsement for dissolving parliament, paving the way for a general election to be held by early July. (published 0427 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par BEIJING ENTERPRISES PRICES TWO-TRANCHE DOLLAR BOND - SOURCE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Beijing Enterprises Holdings Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . has priced a two-tranche dollar-denominated bond, raising $1 billion in the global offering, a person familiar with the offering said Friday. (published 0106 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par FOSUN INTERNATIONAL TO ISSUE $300 MLN BOND DUE 2016 AT 7.5% A YEAR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Fosun International Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Friday it will issue $300 million of five-year bonds at 7.5% a year. (published 0103 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par PHILIPPINES PURISIMA: SAMURAI BOND STILL AN OPTION THIS YEAR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Philippine Finance Secretary Cesar V. Purisima said Friday that the country is still mulling a samurai bond, despite Japan's tragic earthquake, while a global peso offering could also be an option. (published 0443 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par     ======= DOW JONES NEWSWIRES ANALYSIS AND COMMENTARY ======= \par  \par HEARD ON THE STREET: A RATINGS JOLT FOR JAKARTA? \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Jakarta Composite Index gained more than 170% in 2009 and 2010. For the first few weeks of 2011 it slipped back on fears about inflation and potential monetary tightening before recovering, setting new records along the way. Jakarta's average multiple of 2011 earnings is about 15; richer than Thailand's 13 times and the multiple of 14 times in the Philippines. (published 0201 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par CHINA ENERGY WATCH: STATE GIANTS BUILDING UP TECHNICAL PROWESS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China is opening up another front in its campaign to play a greater role in the global energy industry, by honing technical skills to enable it to bid against Western companies for large-scale oil and gas infrastructure projects. (published 0340 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par PREVIEW: TAIWAN APRIL EXPORTS LIKELY REMAINED STRONG \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Taiwan's exports in April likely continued to grow robustly from a year earlier, helped by strong demand for the island's electronics products amid a strong global economic recovery and orders being shifted from Japan following March's earthquake. (published 0311 GMT) [ 06-05-11 0600GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1030 1804 4180   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110506e756000co\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
