% correction, just above 200-day moving average). Resistance at 118.50 (hourly chart); breach would expose upside to 119.77 (yesterday's high), then 120.83 (Wednesday's high), 121.03 (Monday's high) and 121.14 (April 29 high). [ 05-05-11 2338GMT ]\par \par \uc2 EUR/GBP - to trade with bearish bias. Daily chart negative-biased as bearish key-reversal-day pattern completed yesterday; stochastics falling from overbought; MACD staging bearish crossover against its exponential moving average. Support at 0.8861-0.8852 band (yesterday's low-Monday's low); breach would target 0.8842 (April 27 low), then 0.8797 (April 22 low), 0.8779 (April 21 low) and 0.8739 (April 19 reaction low, near 55-day moving average). Resistance at 0.8938 (hourly chart); breach would expose upside to 0.9042-0.9045 band (yesterday's high-March 22, 2010 reaction high), then 0.9133 (March 10, 2010 reaction high) and 0.9148 (March 1, 2010 swing high).\par \par \uc2 -By Jerry Tan, Dow Jones Newswires; (65) 6415-4046; Jerry.tan@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 This is a financial news and information service. It is provided in general terms and does not take account of or address any individual user's position. To the extent that this article includes suggestions as to various possible investment strategies which users might consider, it does so in only general terms without reference to the personal factors which should determine any user's investment decisions. Nothing contained in this service constitutes personalized investment advice. Dow Jones does not warrant the accuracy, completeness or timeliness of the information in this article, and any errors shall not be made the basis for any claim against Dow Jones. The author does not invest in the instruments or markets cited in this article. This article does not constitute or form part of any invitation or inducement to buy or sell any security.\par \par \uc2 [ 05-05-11 2338GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1075 4033   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110505e755001b2\p