\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE: Yen Rally Stokes  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Fears\b0\par\par\uc2 417 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Mai 2011\par 14:33\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 (Rewrites throughout)\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    By Eva Szalay \par    Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 LONDON (Dow Jones)--The yen Thursday surged to its strongest level against the dollar since the Group of Seven major economies last \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to push the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  down in March, stoking fears that another \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  could be just around the corner.\par \par \uc2 The dollar fell below Y80 against the yen in European trading hours, with pre-placed orders driving the pair lower. Widespread investor nervousness also boosted the yen throughout European trading hours, as the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  tends to attract inflows in times of stress.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 -market watchers are now on high alert for tougher rhetoric from Japanese officials over the strength of the yen, particularly as a holiday in the country ends Friday.\par \par \uc2 "The [Y80] level has a clear psychological significance, and has previously been the scene of a tussle between the market and \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's monetary authorities on March 18, 2011. \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  risk is therefore now extremely high," said Gareth Berry, a \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst at \uc2 UBS\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Such a move is unlikely to be imminent, not least as Japanese markets are still on holiday, Berry said. "[But] we must assume that tolerance of yen strength is still very low, and that the \b \highlight22\uc2 ministry of finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  will not hesitate to engage in another round of vigorous \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  if the yen strengthens much further," he said.\par \par \uc2 Derek Halpenny, a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Bank of Tokyo Mitshubishi-UFJ in London, said that a shift below Y78.80 would likely prove to be the trigger for any official action.\par \par \uc2 "There are still lots of speculative long positions in both dollar/yen and euro/yen, so there is a danger of another stop loss driven move lower," Halpenny said.\par \par \uc2 To be sure, at this stage official commentary suggests that there may be more willingness to allow the yen to climb now, compared to last month.\par \par \uc2 The Japanese finance minister said Thursday the current bout of yen strength differs from that in March, in remarks made at a press conference in Vietnam.\par \par \uc2 Nonetheless, analysts are on high alert.\par \par \uc2 "Dollar/yen has continued to grind lower and sits right on the bottom of the pre-quake range. As such, the risk of at least verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the coming sessions is rising significantly," said RBC in a note to clients.\par \par \uc2 At 1152 GMT the dollar was trading at Y79.72.\par \par \uc2 -By Eva Szalay, Dow Jones Newswires; +44 20 7842 9305; eva.szalay@dowjones.com [ 05-05-11 1233GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110505e755000y3\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
