\par\par \uc2 Banker Watch\par \b \uc2 US's Geithner,  \highlight22\uc2 Japan \highlight\uc2 's Noda Didn't Discuss Future  \highlight22\uc2 Forex Intervention \highlight\uc2  - \highlight22\uc2 Japan Ministry Of Finance \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 136 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 April 2011\par 17:34\par \uc2 Dow Jones Top Global Market Stories\par \uc2 DJTGMS\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 WASHINGTON-- Japanese and U.S. finance officials didn't discuss the possibility of future joint \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 -market \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the yen, a Japanese finance ministry official said Friday.\par \par \uc2 "There was no discussion on that matter today," said the official, who was present at the meeting of U.S. Treasury Secretary Timothy Geithner and Japanese Finance Minister Yoshihiko Noda.\par \par \uc2 The official said Noda thanked Geithner for supporting the joint yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  conducted March 18 by the Group of Seven leading industrialized nations.\par \par \uc2 The official added that Geithner told Noda the U.S. economy is faced with various risks but its "expansion is on track."\par \par \uc2 -By Takashi Nakamichi, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-6269-2781; takashi.nakamichi@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJTGMS1120110415e74f0006x\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
