\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE: Japan Finance Minister: G-7 Agrees Joint Action Meaningful When  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Market Volatile\b0\par\par\uc2 636 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 April 2011\par 08:55\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global FX & Fixed Income News\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 --Japan's Finance Minister Yoshihiko Noda said he believes the G-7 agreed on the importance of cooperation during times of volatile \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets\par \par \uc2 --Noda said he called on the G-7 to continue cooperating as appropriate on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy\par \par \uc2 --Noda plans to discuss the G-7's March 18 joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  when he meets U.S. Treasury Secretary Timothy Geithner Friday morning\par \par \uc2 (Adds more comments from Japan's finance minister on the G-7 meeting)\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    By Takashi Nakamichi \par    Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 WASHINGTON (Dow Jones)--The top finance officials of the Group of Seven industrialized nations agreed Friday that \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 -policy cooperation is "meaningful" in times of excessive \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 -market volatility, Japan's finance minister said, something Japanese officials will likely see as a positive outcome, as the yen is once again on the rise.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Assessing the accuracy of Finance Minister Yoshihiko Noda's characterization of the G-7's views is tricky, as the group didn't release the kind of statement it has after past gatherings to showcase its points of agreement. But should Noda's view be accurate, it could discourage speculators from buying the yen too aggressively in times of volatility, with the G-7 standing ready to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  again to ward off sharp yen rises.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Joint yen-selling by the G-7 on March 18 "was an attempt to deal with disorderly movement, excess volatility in the market," Noda told reporters following a meeting of G-7 finance ministers and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  governors. "The measure was effective, as it has successfully curbed such conditions. And I believe we agreed on the view that it is meaningful for the G-7 to cooperate in that kind of situation."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In a separate one-on-one meeting, Noda and European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  President Jean-Claude Trichet also agreed that the concerted \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was successful, a senior Japanese finance ministry official said at a press briefing.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 It is unusual for Japan's finance minister to meet one on one with the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  chief of any country, highlighting Japan's efforts to keep on good terms with the ECB, which largely calls shots on euro-zone \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  had asked for Trichet's time, the official said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Noda plans to discuss the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  with U.S. Treasury Secretary Timothy Geithner during a planned meeting between the two Friday morning, the official added.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Rises in the yen make Japanese products less competitive on the global market, hurting an economy battered by the massive earthquake and tsunami on March 11. Japan's economy relies on exports for much of its growth, as entrenched deflation and a shrinking population have weighed on domestic demand.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The G-7 comprises the U.S., Japan, Germany, France, the U.K., Italy and Canada. The top finance officials met as the yen has been steadily regaining some of the ground it yielded in the aftermath of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The dollar briefly slipped below Y83.00 Thursday. Although that is well above the record low of Y76.25 marked March 17, it is still below the post G-7 \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  high of around Y85.50 on April 6. The U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  stood at Y83.22 at 0640 GMT Friday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Joint \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is usually more effective than \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by individual economies in slowing or reversing the market trend, but it is extremely rare. Last month's move was the first coordinated \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in a decade. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  sought joint action last September when the yen surged, but failed to secure a G-7 deal. It ended up \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  alone to dump the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , according to people familiar with the matter.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Takashi Nakamichi, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-6269-2781; takashi.nakamichi@dowjones.com [ 04-15-11 0255ET ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020110415e74f00048\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
