\par\par \b \uc2 Dow Jones Asia-Pacific Top Stories Sked For April 15\b0\par\par\uc2 2,005 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 April 2011\par 09:11\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 Following are the top Asia-Pacific stories featured on Dow Jones Newswires as of 0700 GMT. Not all stories appear on all wires. Please direct any questions or comments to asianewseds@dowjones.com.\par \par \uc2 MACRO/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 /FIXED INCOME:\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par 3RD UPDATE: CHINA 1ST-QUARTER GDP GROWTH SLOWS SLIGHTLY; MARCH INFLATION RISES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's economic growth slowed slightly in the first quarter, but inflation accelerated to a nearly three-year high in March, raising the likelihood that Beijing will have to take further measures to tighten policy. (published 0429 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: CHINA PRESIDENT HU PLEDGES IMPORT BOOST, EMERGING MARKET INVESTMENT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Chinese President Hu Jintao said Friday the country will boost consumption and imports as part of efforts to restructure its economy, and pledged to invest more in Asian and other emerging markets. (published 0604 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: JAPAN FINANCE MINISTER: G-7 AGREES JOINT ACTION MEANINGFUL WHEN \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  MARKET VOLATILE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The top finance officials of the Group of Seven industrialized nations agreed Friday that \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 -policy cooperation is "meaningful" in times of excessive \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 -market volatility, Japan's finance minister said, something Japanese officials will likely see as a positive outcome, as the yen is once again on the rise. (published 0655 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par INTERVIEW: \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 JAPAN\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  FINANCE MINISTER KEEPS THREAT OF \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  ALIVE \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's finance minister said Thursday he would take "decisive steps" to stabilize the yen if it becomes "excessively volatile," even though the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market had "calmed down" since last month's concerted \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the Group of Seven leading nations. (published 0004 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: JAPAN TURNS FOCUS TO FINANCING QUAKE RECONSTRUCTION \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan turned its focus to financing reconstruction efforts stemming from the devastating March 11 earthquake and tsunami, with ministers Friday floating the possibility of additional bond issuance and a new tax in future. (published 0450 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA JANUARY-MARCH INVESTMENT IN REAL ESTATE DEVELOPMENT UP 34.1% ON YEAR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's statistics bureau said Friday that investment in real-estate development totaled CNY884.6 billion in the January-March quarter, up 34.1% compared with the same period a year earlier. (published 0214 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par DATA SNAP: INDIA PRIMARY ARTICLES WPI UP 1.3% IN WEEK TO APRIL 2 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The wholesale price index for primary articles in India rose 1.3% to 190.6 in the week to April 2, from a provisional 188.2 in the previous week, according to data issued Friday by the Ministry of Commerce and Industry. (published 0639 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par DATA SNAP: INDIA MARCH WHOLESALE PRICE INDEX UP 8.98% ON YEAR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 India's inflation accelerated to 8.98% in March from 8.31% in the previous month, the government said Friday. (published 0626 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA WILL SEEK EVEN BROADER USE OF \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCY\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  -HONG KONG OFFICIAL \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Chinese officials will continue to seek ways to liberalize use of its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and financial markets but it will be quite some time before the yuan mounts a serious challenge to leading reserve \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  such as the U.S. dollar, a U.S.-based Hong Kong official said Thursday. (published 0000 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par HK LEGISLATURE APPROVES CONTROVERSIAL BUDGET AFTER 2-DAY DEBATE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 After a two-day marathon debate, Hong Kong's legislature Thursday approved Financial Secretary John Tsang's controversial budget, which includes a HK$6,000 cash handout. (published 0157 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: TAIWAN PASSES LUXURY TAX BILL, STEPS UP FIGHT ON INFLOWS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Taiwan's legislature on Friday passed a bill introducing a luxury tax partly aimed at reining in home prices, as the island steps up efforts to fight inflation pressures spurred by capital inflows. (published 0605 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: S KOREA FSC TO ANNOUNCE HOUSEHOLD DEBT MANAGEMENT PLAN IN 2Q \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korea's Financial Services Commission Chairman Kim Seok-dong Friday said the regulator plans to announce a comprehensive plan to manage systemic risks posed by growing household debt in the second quarter. (published 0506 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: PHILIPPINES FEBRUARY REMITTANCE $1.50 BLN, UP 6.2% ON YEAR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Filipinos living and working overseas sent home $1.50 billion in February, up 6.2% from the $1.41 billion posted in the same month a year earlier, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said Friday, citing preliminary data. (published 0629 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par PREVIEW: SINGAPORE MARCH NON-OIL DOMESTIC EXPORTS LIKELY GREW 4.7% ON YEAR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Exports of goods produced in Singapore likely eased in March because of lower demand for electronics, analysts say, even as they caution that the data could surprise on the positive side after the government reported that gross domestic product soared in the first quarter. (published 0439 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par PREVIEW: NEW ZEALAND 1Q CPI LIKELY UP 1.0% ON QUARTER, PUSHED UP BY FUEL \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 New Zealand's consumer price index likely continued to accelerate in the first quarter from the previous quarter, largely on the back of higher fuel and food prices. (published 0319 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 EQUITIES:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: SHANGHAI INDUSTRIAL TO SELL 59% STAKE IN SHANGHAI URBAN DEVELOPMENT FOR HK$6.11 BLN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Shanghai Industrial Holdings Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Thursday it agreed to sell its entire stake in a Chinese property firm to its affiliate \f28 \uc2 \f2 Shanghai Industrial Urban Development Group Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . for HK$6.11 billion . (published 0213 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: KDB TO RESTART DAEWOO SHIPBUILDING SALE WHEN MARKET CONDITIONS PERMIT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Korea Development Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2  Chief Executive Kang Man-soo said Friday that the bank will restart the sale of its stake in \f28 \uc2 \f2 Daewoo Shipbuilding & Marine Engineering Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . when market conditions permit. (published 0212 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 GM KOREA\f28 \uc2 \f2 : SUZUKI MOTOR SELLS ENTIRE 6.83% STAKE IN COMPANY TO GM \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Suzuki Motor Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . has sold its entire 6.83% stake in \f28 \uc2 \f2 GM Korea Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . to parent company \f28 \uc2 \f2 General Motors Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . for KRW110 billion, the South Korean unit of the Detroit-based car maker said Friday. (published 0158 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CAPITALAND: UNIT BUYS 40% STAKE IN TEMASEK-OWNED SURBANA FOR S$360 MLN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 CapitaLand Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Friday its unit is buying a 40% stake in Surbana Corp., a unit of Singapore sovereign wealth fund \f28 \uc2 \f2 Temasek Holdings Pte. Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., for S$360 million. (published 0036 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par HANA FINANCIAL 1Q NET PROFIT KRW389.47 BLN; BETTER THAN EXPECTED \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korea's \f28 \uc2 \f2 Hana Financial Group Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2 . Friday said first quarter net profit fell 2.6% from a year earlier, beating market expectations due to strong results from the lender's key \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . (published 0642 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: KOREAN PORTALS FILE COMPLAINT AGAINST GOOGLE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korean search portals Naver and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Daum Communications Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . Friday filed a complaint with the country's Fair Trade Commission against \f28 \uc2 \f2 Google Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2 . for allegedly limiting their access to smartphones using the Android operating system. (published 0521 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par AU OPTRONICS, SHARP DROP LAWSUITS, SIGN PATENT-SHARING AGREEMENT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 AU Optronics Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Sharp Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said in a joint statement Friday they will drop all the pending lawsuits the companies filed against each other and sign an agreement to share some liquid-crystal-display patents. (published 0622 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: NZ TOURISM HOLDINGS FACES PARTIAL TAKEOVER OFFER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 New Zealand-based investment company Ballylinch LP Friday offered to buy a further 40.85% stake in New Zealand's \f28 \uc2 \f2 Tourism Holdings Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., in a deal worth around NZ$28 million . (published 0351 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par BORAL ACQUIRES WAGNERS GROUP ASSETS IN QUEENSLAND FOR A$173M \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Boral Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Friday it is buying assets from fellow Australian construction materials company Wagners Group for 173 million Australian dollars . (published 2258 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par RIO TINTO REITERATES GOAL OF ORGANIC GROWTH, ACQUISITIONS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Anglo-Australian mining company \f28 \uc2 \f2 Rio Tinto PLC\f28 \uc2 \f2 , fresh from securing control of coking coal producer \f28 \uc2 \f2 Riversdale Mining Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., has committed itself to further acquisitions in addition to organic growth. (published 0247 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: PALADIN CUTS FY OUTPUT GUIDANCE; SAYS NUCLEAR POWER SAFE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Uranium miner \f28 \uc2 \f2 Paladin Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . on Friday stepped up its criticism of international media's reporting on the unfolding nuclear crisis in Japan, saying it is "obsessed" with the incident and that nuclear power is inherently safe. (published 0403 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par OM HOLDINGS TO MOVE PRIMARY LISTING TO HONG KONG \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Manganese miner \f28 \uc2 \f2 OM Holdings Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . will move its primary listing to the Hong Kong stock exchange as part of its plans to dual-list in the territory, the company said Friday. (published 2249 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par ANGANG STEEL: EXPECT 1ST-QUARTER NET PROFIT CNY71 MLN; DOWN 94% ON YEAR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Chinese steel maker Angang Steel Co. said Thursday it expects its first-quarter net profit to fall by 94% from a year earlier due to a significant increase in raw material and fuel prices. (published 0013 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: INDIA ENVIRONMENT MINISTRY HOLDS BACK OK TO POSCO STEEL PLANT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korean steelmaker Posco has hit another roadblock with its already five-year delayed proposed steel plant in eastern India with the environment minister late Thursday asking the Orissa state government to settle the claims of two villages on site before giving the $12-billion project a crucial forest clearance. (published 0555 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 INFOSYS TECHNOLOGIES\f28 \uc2 \f2  4TH QUARTER NET PROFIT RISES ABOUT 14% TO INR18.18 BLN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Infosys Technologies Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . Friday posted a nearly 14% rise in its fourth-quarter consolidated net profit and forecast an 18%-20% dollar revenue growth this fiscal year as demand for outsourcing technology services booms. (published 0413 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par TEPCO: HOPE TO PAY PRELIMINARY COMPENSATION TO EVACUEES BEFORE APRIL 29 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Tokyo Electric Power Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . President Masataka Shimizu said Friday the company hopes to start paying initial compensation to evacuees from the area around the stricken Fukushima nuclear plant before the start of the "Golden Week" holidays on April 29. (published 0438 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par QANTAS TO RECOMMENCE DIRECT SERVICE TO TOKYO TUESDAY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 15-04-11 0711GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Qantas Airways Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Friday it will recommence direct services from Sydney to Tokyo on Tuesday following Japan's devastating earthquake, tsunami and related nuclear fallout in March. (published 0608 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ENERGY/COMMODITIES:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: OIL DATA: CHINA MARCH CRUDE OUTPUT 17.57 MLN TONS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China produced 17.57 million metric tons of crude in March, an average of 4.15 million barrels a day, up 4.2% from last March, data from the National Bureau of Statistics showed Friday. (published 0314 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA MARCH COPPER OUTPUT HITS NEW HIGH; 2011 OUTLOOK BULLISH \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's March copper output rose to a record high as ample concentrate supply allowed smelters to keep production running at almost full capacity amid higher global prices, while aluminum output continued to post gains, compared with the previous month and from a year earlier, after producers restarted idled capacity late last year and new capacity came online in the first quarter. (published 0623 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: CHINA MOVES TO CAP BASE METAL OUTPUT CAPACITY GROWTH \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China has capped the annual output capacity growth rate for 10 types of nonferrous metals at an average of 8%, marking the latest state-level push to cull overcapacity in the country's energy-intensive metal industry. (published 0603 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA 1ST QTR NATURAL GAS IMPORTS 6.3 BLN CUBIC METERS, DOUBLE ON YR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China imported 6.3 billion cubic meters of natural gas in the January-March period, more than double the volume of imports a year earlier, the National Development & Reform Commission said Friday. (published 0408 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: VENEZUELA AND VIETNAM PLAN REFINERY EXPANSION, PRODUCT SALES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Petroleos de Venezuela SA\f28 \uc2 \f2  has agreed with state-run \f28 \uc2 \f2 Vietnam Oil and Gas Group\f28 \uc2 \f2 , or \f28 \uc2 \f2 PetroVietnam\f28 \uc2 \f2 , to join a project to upgrade the country's sole refinery and to work together in selling refined oil products in the Asian market, the Vietnam News Agency reported Friday. (published 0514 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: CHINA MARCH CRUDE STEEL OUTPUT RISES 9%, CUES WORRIES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's crude steel output in March rose 9% from a year earlier to 59.42 million metric tons, its second-highest monthly output volume on record, the National Bureau of Statistics said Friday. (published 0258 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: INDIA ENVIRONMENT MINISTRY HOLDS BACK OK TO POSCO STEEL PLANT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korean steelmaker Posco has hit another roadblock with its already five-year delayed proposed steel plant in eastern India with the environment minister late Thursday asking the Orissa state government to settle the claims of two villages on site before giving the $12-billion project a crucial forest clearance. (published 0555 GMT) [ 15-04-11 0711GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 62550   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110415e74f000it\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
