\par\par \b \uc2 *DJ Japan Finance Minister Noda:  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Market Has Calmed Down Since Joint G-7 Action\b0\par\par\uc2 585 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 April 2011\par 21:36\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2011, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 14 Apr 2011 15:36 EDT *DJ  Noda: Japan Will Take Decisive Steps If Yen Volatility Excessive\par \par \uc2 14 Apr 2011 15:37 EDT *DJ  Japan's Noda: Wouldn't Comment On Yen Levels\par \par \uc2 14 Apr 2011 15:47 EDT *DJ  Japan's Noda: Japan Economic, Social Systems Functioning Well\par \par \uc2 14 Apr 2011 15:48 EDT *DJ  Japan's Noda: Fukushima Nuclear Plant Still In Worrisome State\par \par \uc2 14 Apr 2011 15:48 EDT *DJ  Japan's Noda: Japan Economic, Social Systems Functioning Well\par \par \uc2 14 Apr 2011 15:49 EDT *DJ  Japan's Noda: Govt Will Try To Disseminate Accurate Nuclear Plant Information Quickly\par \par \uc2 14 Apr 2011 15:49 EDT *DJ  Japan's Noda: Fukushima Nuclear Plant Still In Worrisome State\par \par \uc2 14 Apr 2011 15:50 EDT *DJ  Japan's Noda: Govt Will Try To Disseminate Accurate Nuclear Plant Information Quickly\par \par \uc2 14 Apr 2011 16:11 EDT DJ  Japan Finance Minister: Will Take Decisive \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  Steps If Volatility Excessive\par \par \uc2 TOKYO (Dow Jones)--Japan's finance minister said Thursday the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market has "calmed down" since last month's concerted Group of Seven action to curb the yen's strength, but added that the Japanese government will take "decisive steps" if it sees any excessive yen volatility.\par \par \uc2 The comments from Yoshihiko Noda indicate that Japanese authorities remain vigilant on the yen even though they aren't too worried about its moderate rebound over recent trading sessions.\par \par \uc2 Since the rare \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 -market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the G-7 leading industrialized nations on March 18, "basically I'd say that the market has calmed down," Noda told The Wall Street Journal and Dow Jones Newswires in an interview.\par \par \uc2 But Noda said he will request continued cooperation on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy at a planned meeting of G-7 finance ministers and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chiefs later Thursday. He also hinted \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  unilaterally if that becomes necessary because of sharp yen rises.\par \par \uc2 "Our fundamental stance is that if there is excessive volatility or disorderly movement, we will take decisive steps," Noda said.\par \par \uc2 -By Takashi Nakamichi, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-6269-2781; takashi.nakamichi@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 14 Apr 2011 16:12 EDT DJ  Japan Finance Minister: Will Take Decisive \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  Steps If Volatility Excessive\par \par \uc2 TOKYO (Dow Jones)--Japan's finance minister said Thursday the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market has "calmed down" since last month's concerted Group of Seven action to curb the yen's strength, but added that the Japanese government will take "decisive steps" if it sees any excessive yen volatility.\par \par \uc2 The comments from Yoshihiko Noda indicate that Japanese authorities remain vigilant on the yen even though they aren't too worried about its moderate rebound over recent trading sessions.\par \par \uc2 Since the rare \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 -market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the G-7 leading industrialized nations on March 18, "basically I'd say that the market has calmed down," Noda told The Wall Street Journal and Dow Jones Newswires in an interview.\par \par \uc2 But Noda said he will request continued cooperation on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy at a planned meeting of G-7 finance ministers and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chiefs later Thursday. He also hinted \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  unilaterally if that becomes necessary because of sharp yen rises.\par \par \uc2 "Our fundamental stance is that if there is excessive volatility or disorderly movement, we will take decisive steps," Noda said.\par \par \uc2 -By Takashi Nakamichi, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-6269-2781; takashi.nakamichi@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 April 14, 2011 16:12 ET (20:12 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020110414e74e004pu\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
