\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-BOJ Shirakawa: G7  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  action helped stabilise markets\b0\par\par\uc2 297 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 April 2011\par 11:49\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * G7 \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  move prevented negative spillovers -Shirakawa\par \par \uc2 * Adds will ensure market trust in yen is maintained\par \par \uc2 (Adds details, background)\par \par \uc2 TOKYO, April 11 (Reuters) - Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Masaaki Shirakawa said the joint G7 \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stem sharp yen rises in the wake of last month's devastating earthquake played a critical role in stabilising financial markets.\par \par \uc2 Shirakawa also pledged to ensure that trust in Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is maintained by conveying to markets that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will not directly underwrite government debt.\par \par \uc2 "Despite the unprecedented major earthquake and subsequent disasters and despite the fact that Japan's fiscal condition remains severe, it was still possible to issue (government)securities at low interest rates in a stable manner," Shirakawa said in a speech at a seminar on Monday.\par \par \uc2 "This was possible partly because the markets have confidence that the aim of Japan's monetary policy is ... not to facilitate government financing," he told the seminar, hosted by the Institute of Regulation and Risk North Asia.\par \par \uc2 Shirakawa is expected to travel to Washington D.C. to attend this week's gathering of G7 and G20 finance leaders, to be held on the sidelines of the spring IMF meetings.\par \par \uc2 In their first joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  since 2000, the Group of Seven rich nations sold the yen after it spiked to record highs days after the quake, threatening to deal another blow to Japan's export-reliant economy which was picking up from a lull when the disaster struck.\par \par \uc2 Shirakawa said the concerted G7 action not only stabilised exchange-rate moves but helped to prevent negative spillover into the stock market and other markets.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Rie Ishiguro; Editing by Edmund Klamann)\par \par \uc2 JAPAN-ECONOMY/SHIRAKAWA (UPDATE 1)   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020110414e74b000nl\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw200\pich25\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3000\pichgoal375
