\par\par \b \uc2 WSJ(4/7) Yen  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Paying Off\b0\par\par\uc2 581 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 April 2011\par 09:53\par \uc2 Dow Jones Chinese Financial Wire\par \uc2 DJCFWE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright (c) 2011, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 The yen's fall to its lowest level against the dollar and the euro in months is the latest sign that a coordinated post-earthquake \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is working.\par \par \uc2 But how low can the yen go?\par \par \uc2 The dollar was buying more than &yen;85 during the Asian trading day Wednesday. That amounts to a 7% decline for the yen since the Group of Seven industrialized nations announced a coordinated bout of yen selling on March 18, and its weakest level since September, after \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets on its own.\par \par \uc2 In morning U.S. trading Wednesday, the dollar was at &yen;85.30, up from &yen;84.83 late Tuesday in New York. The euro was at &yen;122.29 from &yen;120.64. A day before the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the dollar was at around &yen;78.95 and the euro was at around &yen;110.70.\par \par \uc2 "This is shaping up to be one of the most successful episodes of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  ever," says Sean Callow, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist for Westpac Institutional Bank in Sydney.\par \par \uc2 The euro hit an 11-month high against the yen in Asia on Wednesday, thanks to the increasingly divergent paths being set by monetary authorities in the two economies. The European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is widely expected to raise interest rates at a meeting Thursday. Higher interest rates generally attract capital.\par \par \uc2 The yen's steady drop in recent weeks is encouraging the view that a turning point could finally be at hand for the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  after more than two years of strengthening against the dollar that has frustrated Japanese companies and politicians.\par \par \uc2 Analysts at Nomura say the break of 85 yen "could be significant from a medium-term perspective and we would not be surprised to see a trend of further yen weakness." Nomura has revised its forecast to reflect a further drop in the yen, predicting that the dollar will be buying more than &yen;90 in 2012 as U.S. interest rates rise and \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rates remain anchored.\par \par \uc2 The success of the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is partly explained by traders who now see a ceiling on yen strength, thanks to the threats of future \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . That has given investors confidence to pile into so-called carry-trade bets, in which they borrow yen at very low interest rates and convert that cash into higher-yielding \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  such as the Australian dollar, which is also trading at recent highs against the yen.\par \par \uc2 Another factor is Japan's weakened economic condition. Rolling electricity blackouts and nuclear fears are hampering manufacturing and exports. Even a temporary disruption could lessen the demand for Japanese automobile, technology and machinery companies to convert money earned abroad back into yen.\par \par \uc2 Standard Chartered dropped its 2011 Japan growth forecast from 1.9% to 0.7% this year. It raised its 2012 forecast in expectation of a strong V-shaped recovery, and figures the dollar will strengthen to &yen;90.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the Bank of Japan was scheduled to meet Thursday and is under pressure to further loosen monetary conditions by expanding its asset-purchase program to support Japan's post-earthquake recovery, a move that would naturally depress the yen by increasing its supply.\par \par \uc2 A weaker yen should help embattled Japanese companies coping with the aftermath of twin natural and nuclear disasters, and continued supply and electricity shortages.\par \par \uc2 -By ALEX FRANGOS\par \par \uc2 -0-\par \par \uc2 Copyright (c) 2011 \uc2 Dow Jones & Company, Inc\uc2 . \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJCFWE0020110408e747009c5\par }\par \b \uc2 Zusammenfassung der Suche\b0\par \par  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Text\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50\uc2 (foreign exchange or fx or forex or currenc*) and (interven* or operation*) and (japan near10 interven*) and (rst=trtw or rst=tprw or rst=tdjw) and (central bank or ministry of finance or treasury ministry or monetary authority)\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 {  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\row } \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Datum\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50\uc2 01/01/1995 bis 21/08/2023\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 {  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\row } \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\cl